## Original User Request
**Description**: Investigate existing local artifacts to build a coverage matrix and artifact inventory that determines what's already covered before any new tool/skill is built. Scope: (a) Read the role definition doc to extract §4.1 runbooks, §4.2 eval frameworks, §4.3 query patterns, §5.1, §5.3, §6 SOP-1/2/3, §7 deploy row, §10.2/§10.4/§10.5, §11.1/§11.2/§11.3 — these define the source-of-truth workflows and reference docs. (b) Enumerate every currently exposed MCP tool/skill (atlassian, bitbucket, teamwork_graph, compass, switcheroo, socrates, slack, loom, rovodev, feedback, tap, s360, google_calendar, google_drive, gmail, etc.) by reading each SKILL.md / tool.json / reference docs, and map each capability to candidate ML operations from the 13 proposed tools. (c) Inspect the `responsible-ai-api` reference codebase (§5.3) for reusable patterns: circuit breaker, rate limiting, kill-switches, canary deploy, detectors-as-code, ML auth/client base. (d) For each of the 13 proposed tools (mlflow-run, ml-registry-tarot, ml-studio-job, feature-store-mlfs-tecton, ml-lens-query, signalfx-detector-iac, teamserve-deploy, sagemaker-endpoint, ai-gateway-routing, rovo-eval-runner, aix-eval-runner, pir-drafter, orbit-context-bind, symphony-autonomy-check) produce a Coverage row: Already-Covered / Partial-Covered / None — with evidence pointers. (e) For each of the 7 proposed skills (ml-experiment-lifecycle, ml-drift-triggered-retraining, ml-incident-response, ml-deployment-manifest, ml-launch-review-checklist, ml-runbook-authoring, ml-evaluation-rigor) list the existing tools the skill will invoke and the available commands relevant to each workflow step. (f) Inventory canonical reference docs/runbooks/templates/dashboards listed in §11.2 + §4.1 as operational artifacts.

