## 4. Atlassian's Production Cost Anomaly Detection Algorithm (Current State)

### What it is
The production anomaly detection system at Atlassian uses a **multi-check consensus model** where ALL checks must agree on anomaly type (spike or drop) to flag an anomaly.

### How it works —5-Check Consensus Model

| Check | Method | Parameters |
|-------|--------|------------|
| ①Prophet forecast | Facebook Prophet time-series model, 95% CI, ~10 weeks history | Weekly frequency, confidence interval = 95% |
| ② Extremity ranking | Latest week in top/bottom 2 of historical dataset | Rank = 2 |
| ③ Rolling % change | Current week vs. average of previous N weeks | Spike: +40%, Drop: -40%, Window: 4 weeks |
| ④ Rolling absolute change | Current week vs. average of previous N weeks | Spike: +$500, Drop: -$500 |
| ⑤ Standard deviation | Current week vs. N-week distribution | Outside X standard deviations |

**Dimension-specific thresholds:**
| Dimension | Spike % | Spike $ | Lookback |
|-----------|---------|---------|----------|
| AWS Region | 20% | $500 | 4 weeks |
| AWS Product | 40% | $500 | 4 weeks |
| Service Group | 40% | $500 | 10 weeks |
| Service ($500-$10K) | 60% | $3,000 | 10 weeks |
| Service (>$10K) | — | $3,000 | 10 weeks |

**Slow change detection** (supplement):
- `slow_change_check`: Consistent increase/decrease over 3-week window, >$3,000 diff between week 1 and 3
- `slow_change_stable_check`: >10% increase weekly for≥20% of10-week periods
- `slow_change_linear_check`: Linear regression to detect consistent trends

### Severity Classification
```python
# SEV-3: wow_delta > $11,500and< $57,700 (spike)
# SEV-2: wow_delta >= $57,700 (spike)
# Where: wow_delta = cost_recent_week - average_weekly_cost_over_10_weeks
```

### Operational Severity Matrix (Cost Incident Program)
| Cost Anomaly | Time | Sev 3 | Sev 2 |
|-------------|------|-------|-------|
| Cost Spike | Any | >$8K/week | >$40K/week |
| Unresolved >7 days | TTR exceeded | >$3K/week | — |

### How it applies to SKILL.md
For ML experiment cost stewardship, adapt the tiered threshold approach:
- **Micro experiments** ($0-$500/day): Higher % threshold (80%), lower absolute ($30)
- **Small experiments** ($500-$2K/day): 60% threshold, $70 absolute
- **Medium experiments** ($2K-$10K/day): 40% threshold, $215 absolute
- **Large experiments** ($10K-$50K/day): 35% threshold, $430 absolute
- **Very large experiments** (>$50K/day): 25% threshold, $715 absolute

The AI employee should use the multi-check consensus approach (at least 2-3 independent signals agreeing) to reduce false positives.

**Source**: [Current Cost Anomaly Detection Mechanism [In Review]](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CFINOPS/pages/5330060104)

