## Finding 9: Governance Tier Actions Matrix

### What it is
A mapping of what specific actions the AI employee may take at each governance tier, derived from Atlassian's FinOps action patterns.

### How it works

| Action Category | 🟢 Autonomous | 🟡 Propose + Confirm | 🔴 Require Sign-off |
|----------------|---------------|---------------------|---------------------|
| **Monitoring** | Configure alerts, create dashboards, generate reports | Modify alert thresholds, add new detectors | Change SLO definitions |
| **Reporting** | Generate anomaly reports, cost breakdowns | Send notifications to Slack channels | Escalate to leadership |
| **Scaling** | Recommend scale-down (non-production, after hours) | Scale-down idle training jobs (with15-min delay) | Scale-down production inference endpoints |
| **Budget** | Log variance, update forecasts | Reallocate within team budget envelope | Cross-team budget transfer, request new budget |
| **Training Jobs** | Add cost annotations, tag experiments | Pause exploration runs that plateaued | Terminate active training runs |
| **Commitments** | Report utilization of existing commitments | Propose RI/SP purchases | Purchase commitments |
| **Infrastructure** | Rightsizing recommendations | Submit rightsizing PRs (non-production) | Submit infrastructure PRs (production) |

### How it applies
This directly encodes into the SKILL.md as the "action authority matrix" — the AI employee checks the matrix before taking any action to determine whether it can proceed autonomously, propose-and-wait, or escalate.

**Source**: Synthesized from [FinOps: Optimisation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CFINOPS/pages/3626633885), [Cost optimization automated guardrails](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120205103ba513d5e474d91030aa05e16f95f/pages/6871877040), [Agentic Operations](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6885869718)

