    - "Unknown → red (silence is never the default)"
    - "Irreversible action → always red"
    - "Dual gate: must pass BOTH % AND $ check for green"
    - "Stacking: 3+ concurrent yellows → red"
    - "Runaway (< 1h to exhaustion) → immediate red regardless of amount"
```

---

## Key Architectural Decision: Configurable Thresholds with Organizational Guardrails

Per the Agent Budget Guardrails proposal: **"Local owners can set lower limits, but not exceed organization-approved bounds without explicit override."**

This means:
- Teams can set their own 🟢→🟡 threshold *lower* (e.g., notify at $200/day instead of $500/day)
- Teams CANNOT raise their 🔴 threshold above org maximum without explicit CTO/FinOps override
- Organizational defaults (above) are the starting configuration for all new teams/experiments
- Threshold overrides are version-controlled and auditable

This pattern ensures the AI employee has clear, defensible boundaries while remaining adaptable to different team contexts and budget sizes.[0m
