## 13. How This Applies to Skill/Tool Specification

### For Tool Surfaces (Executable Operations)
An AI employee tool wrapping Tarot v3 should expose these key operations:

1. **`registry_register_component`** — Create namespace + component + permissions in one idempotent call
2. **`registry_upload_and_version`** — Upload artifacts + create version (two-step upload + version creation)
3. **`registry_query_component`** — Get component by name/UUID, list versions, get version details
4. **`registry_promote_version`** — Create alias or tag on a version + optionally trigger Deployment Store replication
5. **`registry_check_compliance`** — Query DMP status of an artifact ARI before deployment
6. **`registry_get_lineage`** — Trace lineage graph for a component version

### For SKILL.md Workflow Guidance
- **Human confirmation required**: Before promoting to production (alias creation + deployment store trigger), before deleting components/versions
- **Autonomous execution safe**: Querying components, listing versions, reading lineage, checking compliance status
- **Key terminology**: Namespace, Component, Version, Artifact, Tag (mutable), Alias (immutable), Label, Annotation, Compliance, Data Classification, Attribution, DMP Attestation, Dreamcatcher (lineage)

### Rate Limits & Constraints
- Artifact upload size: 156 GB cap (v2); no documented cap for v3 but chunked
- Version tags: 25 chars max, alphanumeric + minus
- Version immutability: Once created, versions cannot be modified (only labeled/annotated)
- Tag immutability: Tags CAN be moved; aliases CANNOT
- Tarot versions are immutable —409 Conflict if you try to re-register an existing version tag

