─── Response ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Read tool schemas live for s360, socrates, compass, switcheroo,
teamwork_graph, rovodev, bitbucket and the TWG SKILL.md/COMMANDS.md. Output
written to outputs/facet.md.

Key findings:

 1 socrates is the ONLY data plane for cost numbers — schema-agnostic async
   SQL (create_query → get_query_status). No table discovery or curated
   semantics.
 2 s360 is the wrong domain (GTM revenue, not infra cost). Eliminated.
 3 compass provides component identity/attribution only (custom fields,
   ownerIds as Team ARI, deployments) — no cost/$ fields. Use as join key.
 4 switcheroo is an operational lever (scale-down/kill-switch flags) but
   cost-blind — referenced from runbooks, not bundled.
 5 teamwork_graph is identity/org-rollup (Cypher + 50+ helpers) — no cost
   nodes in the ontology per METAGRAPH.md / NATIVE-SURFACES.md.
 6 rovodev.atlassian_search (ORCHESTRATOR) + CQL search are the discovery
   surfaces for FinOps pages/runbooks/post-mortems.
 7 bitbucket.bitbucketRepoContent.files.get retrieves IaC/TEAMServe/Spinnaker
   manifests — useful inputs for the migration analyzer.
 8 TWG SKILL has no FinOps surface; Cypher fallback won't find cost data.

Coverage matrix for the 3 proposed tools:

 • ml-cost-query → Partial: socrates execution exists; gap = curated SQL
   templates + table registry + cost-unit normalization.
 • gpu-quota-tracker → Largest gap: no MCP exposes a quota system of record.
   Must locate via Confluence/Bitbucket search.
 • infra-migration-analyzer → Gap: no MCP — but it's a synthesis/reporting
   tool that reuses socrates + compass + twg + bitbucket as inputs and
   atlassian/jira for publication.

Validated Confluence pointer: MOI Gaps for Non LLM Cost for AI Cost Centre
(page id 7083638717) explicitly references AWS as vendor and Cost Centre 2006
(Engineering-AI) — strongest single starting point for canonical cost
tables/dimensions. The §5.3 SageMaker→TEAMServe $5.6M / 59% savings
post-mortem and the GPU-quota service of record were NOT located by my CQL
searches and remain explicit gaps for sibling/follow-up subtasks.

AI-autonomy notes: All reads are fully autonomous; mutations
(switcheroo.create_*, bitbucket.commit.create,
bitbucketPullRequest.create/merge) require human confirmation per agent SOP.
Socrates async pattern needs bounded poll-with-backoff.


Recommendation: Build cost stewardship as a thin SKILL that (a) wraps socrates
with templated SQL + poll helper, (b) uses compass + teamwork_graph for
attribution, (c) reads IaC from bitbucket, (d) publishes via atlassian/jira,
and (e) owns the 🟢/🟡/🔴 sign-off policy and ROI report schema internally —
none of which exist in any current MCP tool.
