## 9. Agentic CLI Integration (`mlexp`)

### What It Is
An internal CLI tool (`mlexp`) that provides an agentic experiment loop with MLflow integration.

### Key Commands for AI Agent Use
| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `mlexp log --yaml<config> --run-id <id>` | Parse YAML and log a new run |
| `mlexp list [--last N]` | List experiments |
| `mlexp show <id>` | Full detail for one run |
| `mlexp diff<id1> <id2>` | Side-by-side comparison |
| `mlexp sync <id>` | Pull metrics from Databricks |
| `mlexp fetch-mlflow <job_id>` | Fetch MLflow training metrics from a job |
| `mlexp tag <id> baseline` | Tag a run |
| `mlexp track --latest --auto-sync` | Poll until done → sync metrics |

### How It Applies
This CLI represents an existing agentic pattern for experiment management. The AI employee skill could integrate with or extend this CLI for automated experiment tracking, providing:
- Automated run comparison and selection
- Baseline tagging for A/B evaluations
- Automated metric sync and convergence detection

