| Platform | Primary Interface | Auth Model | Key Operations |
|----------|------------------|------------|----------------|
| **ML Studio** | CLI (`atlas ml`) + REST API | ASAP JWT | submit, run, clone, get-status, get-params |
| **Databricks** | SDK (`WorkspaceClient`) + CLI | OAuth2 / API tokens | jobs.run_now, jobs.list, files.upload, MLflow |
| **ML Fabric** | Via ML Studio (transparent) | ASAP → KITT Auth → K8s | PyTorchJob / RayJob creation + monitoring |
| **Optimus Prime** | Databricks notebook + job API | Same as Databricks | Configure sweep, track via MLflow |
| **ML Lens** | Metrics API (native ML Studio integration) | Internal | Emit metrics, configure alerts, dashboards |
| **Praxis** | Python API + CLI | Kubernetes/Kueue | build, run (local/remote) |

**Convergence Diagnostics Taxonomy:**
1. **Loss curves** — train_loss, val_loss per step/epoch (MLflow)
2. **Evaluation metrics** — accuracy, AUC, MRR, F1 at intervals (MLflow)
3. **Hyperparameter search history** — per-trial params + metrics (MLflow experiment)
4. **GPU health** — utilization, memory, NCCL errors (CloudWatch/Splunk/ML Lens)
5. **Job lifecycle** — state transitions, duration, failure reasons (ML Studio Orchestrator DB)
6. **Self-describing artifacts** — JSON files with embedded train_config + eval metrics

