## Finding 6: ML Fabric Intelligent Orchestration Layer (IOL) — Future Direction

### What it is
A proposed unified API layer that abstracts job submission across all cloud providers.

### How it works (proposed)
```
Core Components:
├── Job Submission API (unified interface for all clouds)
├── Resource Orchestration Engine (routing, spot/on-demand/DWS selection)
├── Lifecycle Management (preemption, cleanup)
├── Cost Attribution (per-service UUID tagging)
├── Databricks Token Minting (unified across Praxis, Interactive, ML Studio)
└── Observability (ML Lens or ML Fabric UI)
```

### How it applies
The skill should be forward-compatible with the IOL. Current tool design should use the existing ML Studio API but be structured so that switching to a unified Job Submission API is a parameter change rather than a rewrite.

### Source
- [[Draft Proposal] ML Fabric: Intelligent Orchestration Layer](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6194309469/)

