## 6. Gaps and Future Work

| Capability | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| KS statistic (numeric) | ✅ Available | Auto-computed for MLFS features |
| PSI (binned) | ✅ Available | Stored bin edges in config |
| Chi-squared (categorical) | ✅ Available | Auto-selected by calculator |
| KL Divergence |⚠️ Not explicitly mentioned | PSI is mathematically related; custom emission possible |
| Embedding cosine drift | 🔴 Not platformized | Must compute externally, emit via SDK |
| Online/real-time drift | 🔴 Planned | Currently batch (~5 min cadence) |
| UGC feature drift | 🔴 Out of scope | Requires Kamino → Plato pipeline |
| Anomaly detection (confidence band) | ✅ Available | `algorithm: "confidence_band"` with sensitivity config |

### Key Insight for Tool Design

The ML Lens platform distinguishes between:
1. **Platform-computed drift** (automatic for all MLFS features, no config required)
2. **Custom drift metrics** (teams compute externally, emit via SDK)
3. **Alert subscription** (opt-in, requires explicit config registration)

An AI employee tool should support all three patterns, with the understanding that embedding cosine drift falls under pattern #2 (custom) until the platform builds native support.

