## Practical Patterns for Skill/Tool Encoding

### Pattern 1: Feature Health Check Workflow

```
Step 1: Identify target feature views (by owner, use case, or service)
Step 2: For each feature view, gather:
  - Freshness (time since last write event)
  - Coverage (non-null entity count / total expected entities)
  - Sparsity (null rate per feature column)
  - Drift score (PSI/KS against reference window)
Step 3: Compare against thresholds
Step 4: Generate report with status (PASS/WARNING/ERROR) per dimension
Step 5: If any ERROR → trigger alert or flag for human review
```

### Pattern 2: Online↔Offline Consistency Validation

```
Step 1: Select representative entity sample (production traffic distribution)
Step 2: Record current timestamp as reference point
Step 3: Fetch online features (MLFS read API)
Step 4: Fetch offline features (MLFS offline SDK or Databricks query at same PIT)
Step 5: Join on entity keys
Step 6: Compute per-feature:
  - exact_match_rate
  - mean_absolute_diff
  - p95_relative_diff
  - null_alignment_rate
Step 7: Apply migration readiness gates
Step 8: Report pass/fail with drill-down metrics
```

### Pattern 3: Feature Audit Trail

```
Step 1: For a given feature view, retrieve:
  - Feature definition (schema, producers, consumers, TTL)
  - Write history (correlation IDs → ML Studio job runs)
  - Read access patterns (which services, how frequently)
  - Quality history (null rates, drift scores over time)
Step 2: Cross-reference with SLOs and alerting configuration
Step 3: Identify gaps (missing alerts, no freshness SLO, unconfigured drift thresholds)
Step 4: Generate audit report with recommendations
```

