### 4. Feature Coverage and Sparsity

#### Definitions
- **Coverage**: % of expected entity keys that have non-null feature values
- **Sparsity**: % of null/missing values across feature columns
- **Null Rate**: Per-feature null value percentage

#### MLFS Metrics (current + planned)

**Currently available**:
- Write counts (daily)
- Read counts (daily)
- Failures per feature view
- Row counts

**Planned (Feature Observability Q3-Q4 FY26)**:
| Metric | Online | Offline |
|--------|--------|---------|
| Null value % | ✅ | ✅ |
| Row counts | ✅ | ✅ |
| Join key cardinality & uniqueness | ✅ | ✅ |
| Min/Max/Mean/StdDev (numerical) | ✅ | ✅ |
| Histogram/bins per feature | ✅ | ✅ |
| Data type matching rate | ✅ | ✅ |

**Quality Status Schema (DTI-Ecosystem)**:
```plaintext
quality_status: PASS / WARNING / ERROR
null_rate: float
sparsity_score: float
last_profiled_at: timestamp
last_quality_run_id: string
deprecation_candidate: bool + reason
readiness: not_ready / experimental / ready_for_prod
```

**Feature Quality Profiles Table**:
