```

#### SDK Integration (Planned)

Using `atlassian-ml-dq-sdk` (Data Quality SDK):
- Compute quality metrics (null rates, statistics, PSI, KS) on any PySpark DataFrame
- Emit results to ML Lens
- Default values for basic metrics automatically computed

#### How It Applies to Skill/Tool

A coverage/sparsity check operation should:
1. For a given feature view, pull the latest quality profile (null_rate, row_count, join_key_cardinality)
2. Compare null_rate against threshold (e.g., > 5% → WARNING, > 20% → ERROR)
3. Check coverage = (non-null rows / expected entity count)
4. Report sparsity per feature column
5. Flag features with degraded coverage for investigation

