Authoritative source for the $5.6M/yr / 59% figure: Confluence page 6531298025
— "Teamserve Cost Savings: Self-Managed vs SageMaker" (Pilli Jesus,
2026-02-25). Contains the exact statement: "Teamserve saves ~$5.6M/year (≈59%
cheaper) vs running the same replicas on SageMaker."

Workload basis: 33 models, 615 replicas, 10 regions, projected at 730
hrs/month, effective (post-discount) pricing.

Verified math: Monthly $320,320 (Teamserve) vs $788,459 (SageMaker est.) =
−$468,139/mo → −$5,617,665/yr ≈ 59% reduction.

Top savings drivers: p5en.48xlarge GPU (~$2.48M/yr), g5.2xlarge (~$1.68M/yr),
g6e.xlarge (~$0.64M/yr).

Cost-comparison methodology (machine-readable):

 • Teamserve cost from Bitbucket:
   operations/terraform/model-owners-for-signalfx.json
   (metadata.total_monthly_projected_effective_cost,
   metadata.cost_by_instance_type_effective).
 • SageMaker cost from sagemaker_cost.csv (Databricks export) using
   avg_effective_cost and avg_list_cost.
 • Formula: monthly_cost = hourly_effective_cost × replicas × 730.
 • For instance types with list-only pricing (p5en.48xlarge), apply global
   discount ratio = 0.4916 (avg of effective/list across CSV).
 • Assumptions: 24×7 replicas, full-instance replica equivalence, p5en
   discount estimated from other families.

Model-level case study (supports 50–60% range): Page 6527257073 — "Bluebird 
Migration: 50-60% Cost Reduction with TeamServe". Example: jira-similar-issues
from $5,002/mo (SageMaker) to ~$2,365/mo (TeamServe).

