## E. Recommendation Report Schema

### Finding E1: Best-PracticeFinOps Recommendation Report Schema

**What it is:** A comprehensive schema for an ML infrastructure migration recommendation report, synthesizingFinOps Foundation principles, AWS Well-Architected Cost Optimization pillar, and Google SRE capacity-planning patterns.

**How it works — Complete Schema:**

```yaml
ml_infra_migration_report:
  metadata:
    report_id: string# Unique identifier
    generated_at: datetime     # ISO 8601
    generated_by: string       # AI agent or analyst name
    version: semver            # Schema version
    confidence_level: enum     # high | medium | low
    review_status: enum        # draft | pending_review | approved | superseded
    
  executive_summary:
    recommendation: enum# migrate | defer | investigate_further
    headline_savings_annual: currency# Net annual savings after migration
    payback_period_months: integer
    risk_level: enum           # low | medium | high | critical
    one_line_rationale: string #<100 chars
    decision_deadline: date    # When this analysis expires

  current_state_baseline:
    service_name: string
    current_platform: string   # e.g., "SageMaker on AWS us-east-1"
    monthly_cost_baseline: currency
    cost_trend_90d: enum       # increasing | stable | decreasing
    utilization_avg_pct: float
    workload_characteristics:
      compute_type: enum       # gpu_training | cpu_inference | batch | streaming
      peak_hours_per_day: float
      data_volume_gb_per_month: float
      training_frequency: string# e.g., "daily", "weekly", "on-demand"

  target_state:
    proposed_platform: string  # e.g., "ML Fabric on GCP GKE"
    architecture_changes: list[string]
    expected_monthly_cost: currency
    expected_utilization_pct: float

  financial_analysis:
    cost_comparison:
      baseline_3yr_tco: currency
      migration_costs:
        engineering_effort_weeks: float
        dual_run_period_months: integer
        dual_run_cost: currency
        enablement_training: currency
        total_one_time: currency
      target_3yr_tco: currency
      net_savings_3yr: currency
      
    roi_metrics:
      npv:
        p10: currency          # 10th percentile (pessimistic)
        p50: currency          # 50th percentile (expected)
        p90: currency          # 90th percentile (optimistic)
      irr_pct: float
      payback_period_months: integer
      roi_pct: float           # (Benefits PV - Costs PV) / Costs PV
      
    sensitivity_analysis:
      - variable: string       # e.g., "GPU spot price variance"
        base_value: string
        range: string          # e.g., "±20%"
        npv_impact: currency# Change in NPV per unit change
        is_critical: boolean# True if can flip recommendation
      
    benefit_streams:
      - category: enum# direct_savings | risk_mitigation | productivity | compliance
        description: string
        annual_value: currency
        confidence: enum       # high | medium | low
        evidence: string       # Link or description of supporting data
        risk_adjustment_pct: float  # Probability of achieving (0-100)

  assumptions_register:
    - id: string               # ASM-001, ASM-002, etc.assumption: string
      impact_if_wrong: enum# low | medium | high | critical
      confidence: enum         # validated | estimated | assumed
      validation_method: string
      owner: string
      review_date: date
      
  risk_register:
    - id: string               # RSK-001, RSK-002, etc.
      risk: string
      likelihood: enum         # low | medium | high
      impact: enum             # low | medium | high
      risk_score: integer# 1-10
      mitigation: string
      residual_risk: enum      # low | medium | high
      owner: string
      
  rollback_plan:
    rollback_risk_score: integer  # 1-10 composite
    rollback_risk_factors:
      - factor: string
        score: integer         # 1-10
        rationale: string
    estimated_rollback_cost: currency
    estimated_rollback_time: string# e.g., "2-4 weeks"
    rollback_trigger_conditions:
      - condition: string
        measurement: string
        threshold: stringrollback_procedure_summary: string
    dual_run_duration_recommended: string

  governance_classification:
    tier: enum                 # green_recommend | yellow_reallocate | red_signoff
    rationale: string
    required_approvers: list[string]
    approval_deadline: date
    escalation_path: string

  next_steps:
    - action: string
      owner: string
      due_date: date
      dependency: string       # Optionalappendix:
    data_sources: list[string]
    methodology_notes: string
    comparable_migrations: list[object]  # Prior similar migrations and their outcomes
```

**How it applies:**
- This schema should be the structured output format for the `infra-migration-analyzer` tool.
- The AI agent fills in sections autonomously where data is available, marks sections as "requires_human_input" where it cannot determine values.
- The `governance_classification` section drives the approval workflow.
- The `assumptions_register` enables stakeholders to quickly validate or challenge key inputs.

**Source:** Synthesized from [ROI Evaluation on DX Infrastructure Migration](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/dxip/pages/6377937772); [Epic Overview and Business Case Framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/aats/pages/6460586093); Forrester TEI methodology; AWS Well-Architected Cost Optimization pillar; [Cloud & AI Transformations ROI Prioritization Framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120204c87edae466942a4bf1475e0b0a46281/pages/6928894354)

