## 9. Inference Components (sm-ic-endpoint) — Advanced Scaling

### What it is
SageMaker Inference Components allow independent scaling of models within a shared endpoint.

### How it works

**Two-level scaling:**

1. **Endpoint level (instances):**
   - Option A: Managed Instance Scaling (SageMaker auto-scales based on component needs)
   - Option B: Manual metric-based scaling (same as standard endpoints)

2. **Component level (model copies):**
   ```yaml
   copyCount: 2        # Initial model copies
   min: 1              # Min copies for autoscaling
   max: 5              # Max copies
   cooldown: 300       # Cooldown between scaling
   ```

**Managed Instance Scaling:**
- SageMaker automatically scales endpoint based on inference component needs
- No custom metrics needed
- Only specify min/max instance counts
- During blue-green deploys: enables automatic temporary instance count increase

### How it applies
The tool should differentiate between endpoint-level and component-level scaling when managing inference component resources.

### Source
- [Autoscaling for Inference Components](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/4077551260/Autoscaling+for+Inference+Components)
