## 2. GPU Instance Types & Selection Patterns

### What it is
GPU instance selection for SageMaker endpoints requires balancing throughput, latency, cost, and availability.

### How it works — Instance Type Matrix (Observed at Atlassian)

| Instance Type | GPU | vCPUs | Use Case | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `ml.g4dn.xlarge` | 1x T4 (16GB) | 4 | Light inference, embedding | Available in most regions |
| `ml.g4dn.2xlarge` | 1x T4 (16GB) | 8 | Medium inference | $0.94/hr |
| `ml.g5.xlarge` | 1x A10G (24GB) | 4 | Standard GPU inference | Most common at Atlassian |
| `ml.g5.2xlarge` | 1x A10G (24GB) | 8 | Higher throughput | Sometimes restricted/reserved |
| `ml.g5.4xlarge` | 1x A10G (24GB) | 16 | High throughput (optimal cost profile per research) | 60% more expensive but 4x throughput |
| `ml.g5.12xlarge` | 4x A10G (96GB) | 48 | Large models, high concurrency | Used for search QR models |
| `ml.g6e.4xlarge` | - | - | Next-gen | Availability issues in many regions |
| `ml.p5.48xlarge` | 8x H100 (640GB) | 192 | Very large LLMs | Only in specific AZs |

### Key Optimization Findings

From the "Scaling Smart with SageMaker" blog (Atlassian internal):
- **`SAGEMAKER_MODEL_SERVER_WORKERS`** should be set to the number of vCPUs for GPU instances
- More cores≠ better performance (load testing is essential)
- Upgrading from `g5.xlarge` → `g5.4xlarge` yielded ~4x throughput for only 60% more cost
- `MMS_JOB_QUEUE_SIZE`: Default 100, should be raised (e.g., 200) to buffer during scale-out
- Cost optimization opportunity of **>$2M/year** from proper autoscaling threshold tuning

### How it applies
The tool should include instance type recommendations based on workload profile (model size, request volume, latency target) and check regional availability before recommending changes.

### Source
- [Scaling Smart with SageMaker](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202037d29c9b1fc240f9a0e848ff57d6d77c/blog/2025/08/29/5762103595)
- [SageMaker Learnings](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020919062e0a5a84c57852f705f6efd15b4/pages/3901695186/SageMaker+Learnings+sm-endpoint)

