## 6. Debugging & Monitoring Autoscaling

### What it is
CLI commands and observability patterns for troubleshooting SageMaker scaling failures.

### How it works

**Debug scaling activities:**
```bash
aws application-autoscaling describe-scaling-activities \
  --service-namespace sagemaker \
  --resource-id endpoint/<endpoint-name>/variant/<variant-name> \
  --query "ScalingActivities[?StatusCode!='Successful']"
```

**Common failure response:**
```json
{
  "StatusCode": "Failed",
  "StatusMessage": "Failed to set desired instance count to 30. Reason: The account-level service limit'ml.g5.2xlarge for endpoint usage' is50Instances, with current utilization of 50Instances and a request delta of 24 Instances."
}
```

**Monitoring via SignalFx:**
- Invocations count per endpoint
- InvocationsPerInstance (confirms actual instance utilization)
- ModelLatency (CloudWatch alarm: >5s for 2evaluation periods)
- GPU instance quota usage monitoring (alert near max)

**Formula for verifying instance count:**
```
Actual instances≈ Invocations / InvocationsPerInstance
```

### How it applies
The tool should:
- Query scaling activities for failures
- Check quota limits before recommending scale-out
- Compute current utilization ratio
- Recommend quota increase requests when approaching limits
- Generate SignalFx queries for capacity monitoring

### Source
- [HOWTO: Debug Sagemaker scaling issues](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SER/pages/4030669827/HOWTO+Debug+Sagemaker+scaling+issues)
- [Sagemaker-OSB Reliability Uplift](https://home.atlassian.com/o/2346a038-3c8c-498b-a79b-e7847859868d/s/a436116f-02ce-4520-8fbb-7301462a1674/project/ATLAS-59610)

