## 8. Capacity Planning & Quota Management

### What it is
Patterns for managing GPU instance quotas and reservations across regions.

### How it works

**Quota limits are per-instance-type, per-region:**
- Each AWS account has a limit (e.g., 50 instances of `ml.g5.2xlarge`)
- Scaling will fail with `ResourceLimitExceeded` if quota exhausted
- Quota increases require AWS Support request

**Reservation strategies:**
1. **Targeted capacity reservations** (coming from AWS) — set reservation ID in endpoint config
2. **EC2 → SageMaker conversion** — reserve EC2 instances, coordinate with AWS to convert
3. **Manual coordination** — hold instances with AWS for specific deployments (high-touch)

**GPU availability issues observed:**
- `apse2` (Sydney) and `apne2` (Seoul) have documented GPU scarcity
- `g5.2xlarge` instances sometimes restricted for critical customers
- `g6e` instances not available in many regions
- Reserved instances guarantee availability but pay100% regardless of usage

### How it applies
The tool should:
- Track quota usage per region/instance-type
- Alert when approaching limits (e.g., 80% utilization)
- Factor in blue-green 2x requirement during deployments
- Recommend reservations for critical production endpoints
- Provide fallback instance recommendations when primary type unavailable

### Source
- [DACI: How many SageMaker instances should we reserve in Q4](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/3502051728)
- [2024-03-05 Meeting notes: AWS SageMaker Capacity](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/3456801303)
- [AWS Summit 2024: ML Platform Asks](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~jhansen/pages/4131983923)

