## Stream A (cont.): Micros Service Descriptor Schema

### 8. Micros Service Descriptor — Core Schema

**What it is**: A YAML file that declaratively defines the entire footprint of a Micros service — compute, resources, scaling, deployment strategy, and infrastructure.

**How it works**:

#### Minimum Valid Descriptor:
```yaml
organization: Engineering Services
notifications:
  email: jdoe@atlassian.com
links:
  healthcheck:
    uri: /healthcheck
  source:
    url: https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/my-service
compose:
  microservice:
    image: docker.atl-paas.net/atlassian/my-cool-service
    tag: 0.0.1
    ports:
      - 8080:8080
buildNumber: 0.0.1
```

#### Full Service Descriptor Structure:
```yaml
# Basic settings
name: <SERVICE_NAME>
description: Organization Management
organization: Engineering-Admin Experience
buildNumber: latest
externalAccess: false

# Compute/Container
compose:
  microservice:
    image: docker.atl-paas.net/atlassian/my-service
    tag: "${ARTIFACT_VERSION}"
    ports:
      - 8080:8080

# Tenant context
tenantContext:
  enabled: true

# Health/monitoring links
links:
  healthcheck:
    uri: /healthcheck
  deepcheck:
    uri: /deepcheck
  source:
    url: https://bitbucket.org/atlassian/my-service
  semanticCheck:
    dockerImage:
      name: docker.atl-paas.net/my-service/semantic-checktag: 1.0.0
    splitBy: [group1, group2]

# Scaling configuration
scaling:
  instance:
    - c5.large
  min: 2
  max: 20
  policies:
    scalingOut:
      adjustmentType: PercentChangeInCapacity
      scalingAdjustment: 20minAdjustmentMagnitude: 1scalingAdjustmentSteps:
        - lowerBound: 70
          scalingAdjustment: 20estimatedInstanceWarmup: 300scalingIn:
      adjustmentType: ChangeInCapacity
      scalingAdjustment: 1

# Deployment strategy
deployment:
  type: progressive# or "hot-swap" (deprecated)

# Resources (DynamoDB, SQS, Redis, etc.)
resources:
  - type: postgres-db
    name: db- type: redisx
    name: my-cache
  - type: sqs
    name: eventsattributes:
      SnsTopicSubscriptions:
        - name: my-subscription
          snsTopic: "{{resource service='my-service' type='sns-topic' name='my-topic' property='arn'}}"

# Service proxy / auth
serviceProxy:
  enabled: true

# External compute (KITT++ bridge)
externalCompute:
  securityGroups:
    - groupId: sg-0d466c274609e497b
      accountId: '123456789012'
  trustRelationshipConditions:
    - ouPath: o-rab3nm4fez/*/ou-6ypf-mhairnvs/*
      tags:
        service_name: my-kitt-service

# Environment overrides
environmentOverrides:
  staging:
    scaling:
      min: 1
      max: 5prod:
    scaling:
      min: 5
      max: 50
```

#### Schema Ownership Paths:
| Path | Owner |
|------|-------|
| `$.compute`, `$.compose`, `$.scaling` | Micros Compute Team |
| `$.network` | Core Networks & Automation |
| `$.resources.*.attributes` | Per resource type |
| `$.serviceProxy` | Service to service fabric |
| slauth/poco bits | CloudSec |
| Everything else | Micros Core Team |

#### Validation:
```shell
micros service:validate my-service-name.sd.yml
# OR
atlas micros service deploy --service=$service-name --env=$env -f service-descriptor.yml
```

JSON Schema available at: `go/sdr` (internal link)

**Source**: [Service descriptor reference](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MICROS/pages/167213240), [Copy of Service Descriptor Reference](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~amacheret/pages/564399850), [Service Descriptor & Micros Resources Reference](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ITSOL/pages/6976867502)

---

### 9. Micros Deployment CLI & Progressive Rollouts

**What it is**: The `atlas micros` CLI commands and Spinnaker pipeline integration for deployments.

**CLI Commands**:
```shell
# Deploy service
atlas micros service deploy --service=$name --env=$env -f service-descriptor.yml

# Progressive rollout
atlas micros service deploy -u progressive

# Scale
atlas micros compute scale -s <service> -e <env> --min=<n> --max=<n>

# Resource management
atlas micros resource set -s <service> -e <env> -f service-descriptor.yml

# Validate
micros service:validate my-service.sd.yml
```

#### Progressive Rollout Configuration (Spinnaker Safe Release):
```yaml
pipelines:
- template: safeRelease
  throughput: low
  environments:
    - stg-east
    - prod-east
  disableProgressiveRollouts: false
  progressiveRollout:
    baseGracePeriodMins: 10
    states:
      - percentage: 10
        soakTimeMins: 10- percentage: 50
        soakTimeMins: 15
      - percentage: 100
        soakTimeMins: 0canaryAnalysis:
      enabled: true
      canaryConfigName: <service-name>-canary
      autoRollback: true
```

#### Canary Config (canary-config.yml):
```yaml
name: <service-name>-canary
detectors:
  - type: signalFx
    metric: 5xx_rate
    threshold: 5- type: signalFx
    metric: latency_p99
    threshold: 2000
```

**Source**: [Canary Deployment Implementation Guide](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120203751105336c748498809ee74d33626f3/pages/6372694534), [Evolution of the Micros deployment APIs](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ORCH/pages/2197336764)

---

### 10. Archetype Descriptor (Modern Micros Configuration)

**What it is**: The newer top-level container format that wraps service descriptors, supporting multi-service and multi-environment configurations.

**Structure**:
```yaml
schemaVersion: 1.1.0
id: SERVICE_ID
definitions:
  serviceDescriptor: &base-sd
    ...
  isolationServiceDescriptor: &ic-sd
    ...
serviceSets:
  - name: all
    services:
      - SERVICE_ID
serviceClasses:
  - id: default
    serviceDescriptor: *base-sd
  - id: ic_default
    serviceDescriptor: *ic-sd
    serviceDescriptorOverrides: ...
services:
  - id: SERVICE_ID
    serviceClass: default
    environmentType: ...
```

**Synthesis**: `atlas sliver synth-sd` converts archetype descriptor → flat service descriptor for legacy tools.

**Source**: [RFC054: Archetype Descriptor as source of Helm Values](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KITT/pages/5596449507), [Micros Concepts for my understanding](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020951f2a88bc6c41d0860b7c6d5e169f3e/pages/7000916500)

---

### 11. TEAMServe Service Descriptor Pattern

**What it is**: TEAMServe's self-serve model deployment follows a pattern analogous to Micros service descriptors but using ArgoCD Application YAML + Helm values.

**How it works** (from TEAMServe Digest FY26 Q2):
> "Self-serve model deployment via service descriptor update — For staging/prod models where changes must be checked and tracked for reliability and accountability, TEAMServe will provide access to model owners to add/update new models via Bitbucket commit. This design is similar to specifying service descriptors for SageMaker endpoints."

#### Key fields in TEAMServe "descriptor" (Helm values):
```yaml
# Model identity
model:
  source: ml-registry       # or "tarot", "teamserve"
  group: my-model-group     # model group name
  version: my-model-v1      # version identifier
  s3Bucket: teamserve-model-repository-prod

# Deployment store client (artifact download)
deploymentStoreClient:
  resourceId: "deployment-id"
  target:
    environment: "prod-east"
  model:
    componentRef: "namespace.component.Model"
    versionRef: "1"

# Triton server config
tritonServer:
  args:
    loadModel: "model_name"   # or "*" for all
    enableTracing: true
    modelControlMode: "EXPLICIT"
    exitOnError: true
    metricsIntervalMs: 10000

# Infrastructure
replicas: 5
instanceType: g6e.xlarge
container: "teamserve/nvidia/tritonserver:25.09-py3"
```

**Source**: [TEAMServe Digest FY26 Q2](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202061551fe70fbc403cbc67930b9b879754/pages/5934161839), [Simplified Deployment Store Chart Deployment](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AO2/pages/6608370221)

