### 5. TEAMServe Monitoring/Status API (teamserve-api)

**What it is**: The `teamserve-api` service provides programmatic status, logs, and deployment management.

**How it works**:

#### API Routes:
```
# Model monitoring (live endpoint info)
GET teamserve-api/api/v1/model-monitor/{endpoint-name}/{region}
GET teamserve-api/api/v1/model-monitor/{endpoint-name}# all regions

# Response:
{
  "status": "IN_SERVICE",
  "capacity": 3,
  "instance_type": "g5.xlarge",
  ...
}

# Deployment management (Launchpad)
POST teamserve-api/api/v1/model-deployment# create endpoint
GETteamserve-api/api/v1/model-deployment/{deployment_id}  # status/describe
DELETE teamserve-api/api/v1/model-deployment/{deployment_id}  # delete
```

#### Launchpad SDK (Python):
```python
from teamserve_sdk import TeamServeEndpoint

# Deploy
endpoint = TeamServeEndpoint.deploy(
    component_ref="my-namespace.my-model",
    version_ref="1",
    container="teamserve/nvidia/tritonserver:25.09-py3",
    instance_type="g6e.xlarge",
    container_args={"loadModel": "my_model_name", "exitOnError": True}
)

# Monitor
status = endpoint.get_endpoint_details()
endpoint.info()
endpoint.logs()
endpoint.metrics()
```

**Source**: [[RFC] teamserve-api for model deployments UI](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AO2/pages/6520067116), [Launchpad on TEAMServe User Manual](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AO2/pages/6025226094)

