## 3. Authentication Model

| Method | Usage | Details |
|--------|-------|---------|
| **ASAP tokens** | Production (mandatory) | Atlassian Service Authentication Protocol |
| **SLAuth tokens** | Staging | Service-level auth tokens |
| **JWT (Bitbucket Pipelines)** | Staging CI/CD | Pipeline-based auth |

**Authentication is handled at the ingress level** via Atlassian's Service Proxy (internal network). Consumer services connect to AI Gateway through this proxy — traffic never leaves the VPC.

**Admin access**: For model onboarding/config changes, use SLAuth with group `micros-sv--ai-gateway-dl-admins`:
```bash
atlas slauth token -a mlp-config --groups=micros-sv--ai-gateway-dl-admins -e<env>
```

**Source**: [AI Gateway API Contract v1](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/5795960758), [AI Gateway — Agentic Loops with Tool Use](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202099c5dd7aaf6d47bbbc210f883d8259bb/pages/6819730304)

---

## 4. Required Headers

| Header | Required | Purpose |
|--------|----------|---------|
| `X-Atlassian-UseCaseId` | **Yes** | Registered use case ID (e.g., `confluence-widgets`) |
| `X-Atlassian-CloudId` | **Yes** | Tenant cloud ID for analytics/routing |
| `User-Context` | **Recommended** | UCT token for user identity |
| `Staff-Context` | Alternative | SCT token for internal use cases |
| `X-Atlassian-UserId` | Deprecated | Legacy user identifier |
| `X-Atlassian-Fallback-Strategy` | Optional | `ENFORCED`, `DEFAULT`, `NONE`, `SLO` |

**Critical**: No calls are possible without a whitelisted use case ID. User identifiers drive user-level abuse rate limiting.

**Source**: [AI Gateway API Contract v1](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/5795960758)

---

## 5. Routing Configuration (Policy-Driven Model Routing)

### 5.1 Key Terminology

| Term | Definition | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| **Provider** | Organization that creates the model | OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Amazon |
| **Vendor** | Infrastructure platform serving the model | Vertex AI, Bedrock, OpenAI, TeamServe, Fireworks |
| **Model** | Specific AI model: `provider:modelId` | `openai:gpt-5.5`, `anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6` |
| **Vendor Policy** | Platform-controlled vendor priority/restriction | `only: [vertex, openai]`, `order: [vertex, bedrock]` |
| **Model Override** | Transparent model substitution | `openai:gpt-5.3-> openai:gpt-5.4` |
| **Compatibility Group** | Models shareable across providers at same capability tier | `[openai:gpt-5.4, google:gemini-3-flash]` |

### 5.2 Logical Provider Mapping

| Logical Provider | Vendor Values | Notes |
|-----------------|---------------|-------|
| `openai` | `OPENAI` | Direct OpenAI API |
| `anthropic` | `BEDROCK` (claude-family), `GOOGLE` (claude-family), `ANTHROPIC` | Any vendor hosting Claude |
| `google` | `GOOGLE` (gemini-family) | Google's own models only |
| `meta` | `BEDROCK` (llama-family), `TEAMSERVE` (llama models) | Llama on any host |
| `amazon` | `BEDROCK` (nova-family) | Amazon's own models |
| `deepseek` | `FIREWORKS` (deepseek models) | DeepSeek on Fireworks |
| `atlassian` | `MSP`, `TEAMSERVE` | Always allowed unless blocked |

### 5.3 SLO Registry Configuration

```yaml
slo-registry:
  entries:
    - tier: PRO
      capability: GENERAL
      models:
        - gpt-5.3                # OpenAI
        - anthropic.claude-opus-4-6# Bedrock
        - gemini-3-pro   # Google
        - o4-mini                        # OpenAI (cost-efficient reasoning)
    - tier: STANDARD
      capability: GENERAL
      models:
        - gpt-5.3                        # OpenAI (reasoning disabled)
        - anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5    # Bedrock
        - gemini-3-flash                 # Google
        - gpt-4.1                        # OpenAI (fallback)
    - tier: STANDARD
      capability: CODING
      models:
        - gpt-5.3-codex
        - anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5
        - gemini-3-flash
```

### 5.4 Policy-Driven Routing Milestones (May–September 2026)

| Milestone | Timeline | Capability |
|-----------|----------|------------|
| M0.5 — POC | May 18– June 7 | Prove local routing: `claude-opus-4.6` → `GPT-5.5` |
| M1 — Canonical IDs | June 1 – June 30 | Canonical `provider:modelId`, explainability headers |
| M1.5 — Same-Provider Switch | Late June | Model switch within same provider (e.g., GPT-5.2→GPT-5.5) |
| M2 — Cross-Vendor | June 22 – August 4 | Bedrock↔Vertex (Claude), OpenAI↔Bedrock |
| M3 — Cross-Provider | July 12 – August 8 | Claude↔GPT including reasoning token handling |
| M4 — Model Tiers | August 10 – September | Callers request tier, gateway resolves model |

**Source**: [AI Gateway - Policy-Driven Model Routing - Engineering Overview](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/7001278725)

---

## 6. Fallback & Circuit Breaker Patterns

### 6.1 Current Fallback Mappings

| Primary Model | Fallback Model |
|--------------|----------------|
| OpenAI Chat Completion models | gemini-2.5-flash |
| Bedrock Anthropic Claude models | Google Anthropic Claude models |
| Google Anthropic Claude models | Bedrock Anthropic Claude models |
| Gemini 3 Flash | gemini-2.5-flash |

### 6.2 Fallback Strategy Header

```
X-Atlassian-Fallback-Strategy: ENFORCED | DEFAULT | NONE | SLO
```

- `ENFORCED`: Forces routing to fallback model (useful for testing)
- `DEFAULT`: Automatic platform fallback on failure
- `NONE`: No fallback, consumer handles own retry
- `SLO`: (New) Multi-hop fallback using SLO registry chain

### 6.3 Circuit Breaker Configuration

- **Per-instance, per use-case, per model**
- Opens when failure rate exceeds threshold (5% of requests, minimum 20 calls in 60 seconds)
- States: CLOSED → OPEN → HALF-OPEN
- **Automated fallback enabled by default** for all use cases
- Plan to move to distributed (Redis-backed) circuit breaker for global protection

### 6.4 Internal-Only (AHL/AHM) CloudID Routing

For organizations with `atlassianHostedLLMs = true`:
1. External LLM Validator blocks external routes
2. Automatic fallback to TeamServe (GPT-OSS models)
3. Fallback strategies: `DEFAULT`, `LLAMA_70B`, `GPT_OSS_20B_TS`, `GPT_OSS_120B_TS`, `ENFORCED` (→ Gemini)

**Source**: [AI Gateway Platform Fallback](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/5796071618), [Deep Dive: AI gateway Fallback pattern](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6457728982)

