## 7. Rate Limiting

### 7.1 How It Works

AI Gateway uses **Heimdall** (via Hofund sidecar) for rate limiting:
- **Cost-based rate limiting** (default) — calls Heimdall twice per request: once with estimated cost (pre-request), once with actual cost (post-response)
- Default: **100k TPM (Tokens Per Minute)** per use case per model
- Keys: `client` (ASAP issuer), `tenant` (model ID), `user` (user ID), `ip` (model-ID for TPM), `artifact` (use-case-ID)

### 7.2 Rate Limit Management (CLI)

```bash
atlas ml aigateway usecase ratelimit view -i <use_case_id> -e <environment> -m <model_id>
```

### 7.3 Response Headers on Rate Limit

| Header | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `X-RateLimit-Limit` | Max TPM for use case/model |
| `X-RateLimit-Type` | `MODEL.USE_CASE`, `USER`, `USE_CASE.MODEL.TENANT`, `UPSTREAM` |
| `Retry-After` | Seconds to wait |
| `X-RateLimit-Reset` | Timestamp of limit reset |

**Source**: [AI Gateway Rate Limits](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/6152697444), [AI Gateway Heimdall Decisions](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~70121059708b83b364a50bb46c0251ea64a04/pages/6484558143)

