## Executive Summary

Atlassian's AI Gateway is a **mandatory egress proxy** for all LLM/AI model traffic across the company. It routes requests to OpenAI, Anthropic (via Bedrock/Vertex), Google Gemini (via Vertex), AWS Bedrock (Nova, Llama), and internal self-hosted models (TeamServe/MSP). As of May 2026, it manages **300–400+ use cases**, **204models** across **7 vendors** (OPENAI, BEDROCK, GOOGLE, ANTHROPIC, FIREWORKS, MSP, TEAMSERVE), and is undergoing a major "Policy-Driven Model Routing" evolution (M0.5–M4, May–September 2026).

---

## 1. Architecture Overview

**What it is**: AI Gateway is a Spring Cloud Gateway (Java) service deployed on AWS (primary) and GCP (Bluebird). It sits between all Atlassian product backends and external/internal LLM providers.

**How it works**:
```
Product/Feature (rovo-chat, convo-ai, jira, confluence, etc.)
        │
        ▼
  AI Gateway (Spring Cloud Gateway — Java)
        │── Rate limiting (Heimdall) ── Content moderation ── Auth/Privacy checks
        │┌────┴────────────────────────────────────┐
   ▼                 ▼                        ▼
OpenAI (direct)   Bedrock (AWS)          GCP Vertex AI
GPT-5.xClaude via Bedrock     Claude + Gemini
                  GPT via Bedrock        Chirp-3(speech)
                        │
                        ▼
                  TeamServe (self-hosted)
                  GPT-OSS (vLLM + TRT-LLM)
```

**Key capabilities** (as of May 2026):
- Multi-vendor model routing (OpenAI GPT-5.x, Anthropic Claude via Bedrock+Vertex, Gemini via Vertex, TeamServe internal)
- Unified API (V2) + provider-specific passthrough (V1)
- Per-use-case rate limiting via Heimdall (cost-based, token-based)
- Cross-vendor fallback with circuit breakers
- Tenant-aware routing (AHL/AHM customers never hit external LLMs)
- Responsible AI content moderation filter
- Cost tracking and attribution
- Priority routing (OpenAI Priority Tier, upcoming Gemini PT)

**Source**: [Atlassian AI Gateway: Deep Research Report (May 2026)](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120203d68974c84a8453ab01c35740e7b4416/pages/7068910538)

---

## 2. API Endpoints — Full Surface

### 2.1 V1 Provider-Specific Endpoints (Primary, Not Deprecated)

| Provider | Endpoint Pattern | Examples |
|----------|-----------------|----------|
| OpenAI | `/v1/openai/{endpoint}` | `/v1/openai/v1/chat/completions`, `/v1/openai/v1/responses` |
| Google | `/v1/google/{endpoint}` | `/v1/google/v1/publishers/google/models/{model}:generateContent` |
| Bedrock | `/v1/bedrock/{endpoint}` | `/v1/bedrock/model/{modelId}/invoke` |
| TeamServe | `/v1/teamserve/{modelId}` | Direct access to internal infrastructure |
| MSP | `/v1/msp/*` | MSP-hosted models |

**Base URLs**:
- Production: `https://ai-gateway.prod-east.atlassian.io`
- Staging: `https://ai-gateway.stg-east.atlassian.io`

### 2.2 V2 Unified API (Model-Agnostic)

**Endpoint**: `POST /v2/chat`

**Request structure**:
```json
{
  "platform_attributes": {
    "model": "gpt-5.3",
    "fallback": {
      "model": "gemini-3-flash",
      "strategy": "ENFORCED"// ENFORCED | DEFAULT | NONE
    },
    "additional_request_fields": {
      "gpt-5.3": {
        "$.reasoning": {"effort": "high"}
      }
    },
    "additional_response_fields": {
      "gpt-5.3": ["$.usage.reasoning_tokens"]
    }
  },
  "request_payload": {
    "messages": [
      {"role": "system", "content": "..."},
      {"role": "user", "content": "..."}
    ],
    "tools": [...],
    "tool_choice": "auto",
    "temperature": 0.7,
    "max_completion_tokens": 4096,
    "stream": true,
    "response_format": {"type": "json_schema", "json_schema": {...}}
  }
}
```

**Response structure**:
```json
{
  "platform_attributes": {
    "model": "gpt-5.3",
    "vendor": "openai"
  },
  "response_payload": {
    "choices": [{
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "index": 0,
      "message": {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "..."
      }
    }],
    "usage": {
      "input_tokens": 100,
      "output_tokens": 50,
      "total_tokens": 150
    }
  }
}
```

**Source**: [AI Gateway API Contract V2 (Beta)](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/5796018590), [Announcing the Unified API](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/blog/2025/10/31/6019777860)

### 2.3 V2 SLO-Based Routing (Target State — In Development)

```json
{
  "platform_attributes": {
    "routing": {
      "tier": "STANDARD",        // PRO | STANDARD | LIGHT
      "capability": "GENERAL",   // GENERAL | CODING | VISION | IMAGE_GEN
      "preferred_model": "gpt-5.3"
    }
  },
  "request_payload": { "messages": [...] }
}
```

**Response headers for routing explainability**:
```
X-Model-Used: gpt-5.3
X-Provider-Used: openai
X-Routing-Tier: standard
X-Routing-Capability: general
X-Routing-Preferred-Model: gpt-5.3
X-Routing-Was-Preferred: true
X-Routing-Fallback-Attempts: 0
```

**Source**: [(Draft) SLO-Driven Model Router](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020f435e62f8b0944b59f3bd4c2d2bb26ed/pages/6562981469)

### 2.4 V2 Invoke (Pass-Through — New)

```json
POST /v2/invoke
{
  "platform_attributes": {
    "endpoint": "CHAT_COMPLETIONS",  // CHAT_COMPLETIONS | MESSAGES | GENERATE_CONTENT
    "preferred_model": "gpt-5.3",
    "fallback_model": "claude-sonnet-4-5"
  },
  "request_payload": {
    // Provider-native request payload (opaque to gateway)
  }
}
```

**Response** includes resolved metadata:
```json
{
  "platform_attributes": {
    "resolved_model": "claude-sonnet-4-5",
    "resolved_provider": "BEDROCK",
    "resolved_endpoint": "MESSAGES",
    "preferred_model": "gpt-5.3",
    "fallback_used": true
  },
  "response_payload": { /* raw provider response */ }
}
```

**Source**: [M1: /v2/invoke Model API (Pass-Through)](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6679544726)

### 2.5 OpenAI Responses API (Compatible Route)

```
POST /v1/openai/v1/responses
```

Supports the newer OpenAI Responses API format directly via the OpenAI-compatible route, with `reasoning` parameters and streaming support.

**Source**: [AI Gateway quick start 'hello world'](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/loomhq/pages/5922572981)

