## 5. Routing Configuration (Policy-Driven Model Routing)

### 5.1 Key Terminology

| Term | Definition | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| **Provider** | Organization that creates the model | OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Amazon |
| **Vendor** | Infrastructure platform serving the model | Vertex AI, Bedrock, OpenAI, TeamServe, Fireworks |
| **Model** | Specific AI model: `provider:modelId` | `openai:gpt-5.5`, `anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6` |
| **Vendor Policy** | Platform-controlled vendor priority/restriction | `only: [vertex, openai]`, `order: [vertex, bedrock]` |
| **Model Override** | Transparent model substitution | `openai:gpt-5.3-> openai:gpt-5.4` |
| **Compatibility Group** | Models shareable across providers at same capability tier | `[openai:gpt-5.4, google:gemini-3-flash]` |

### 5.2 Logical Provider Mapping

| Logical Provider | Vendor Values | Notes |
|-----------------|---------------|-------|
| `openai` | `OPENAI` | Direct OpenAI API |
| `anthropic` | `BEDROCK` (claude-family), `GOOGLE` (claude-family), `ANTHROPIC` | Any vendor hosting Claude |
| `google` | `GOOGLE` (gemini-family) | Google's own models only |
| `meta` | `BEDROCK` (llama-family), `TEAMSERVE` (llama models) | Llama on any host |
| `amazon` | `BEDROCK` (nova-family) | Amazon's own models |
| `deepseek` | `FIREWORKS` (deepseek models) | DeepSeek on Fireworks |
| `atlassian` | `MSP`, `TEAMSERVE` | Always allowed unless blocked |

### 5.3 SLO Registry Configuration

```yaml
slo-registry:
  entries:
    - tier: PRO
      capability: GENERAL
      models:
        - gpt-5.3                # OpenAI
        - anthropic.claude-opus-4-6# Bedrock
        - gemini-3-pro   # Google
        - o4-mini                        # OpenAI (cost-efficient reasoning)
    - tier: STANDARD
      capability: GENERAL
      models:
        - gpt-5.3                        # OpenAI (reasoning disabled)
        - anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5    # Bedrock
        - gemini-3-flash                 # Google
        - gpt-4.1                        # OpenAI (fallback)
    - tier: STANDARD
      capability: CODING
      models:
        - gpt-5.3-codex
        - anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5
        - gemini-3-flash
```

### 5.4 Policy-Driven Routing Milestones (May–September 2026)

| Milestone | Timeline | Capability |
|-----------|----------|------------|
| M0.5 — POC | May 18– June 7 | Prove local routing: `claude-opus-4.6` → `GPT-5.5` |
| M1 — Canonical IDs | June 1 – June 30 | Canonical `provider:modelId`, explainability headers |
| M1.5 — Same-Provider Switch | Late June | Model switch within same provider (e.g., GPT-5.2→GPT-5.5) |
| M2 — Cross-Vendor | June 22 – August 4 | Bedrock↔Vertex (Claude), OpenAI↔Bedrock |
| M3 — Cross-Provider | July 12 – August 8 | Claude↔GPT including reasoning token handling |
| M4 — Model Tiers | August 10 – September | Callers request tier, gateway resolves model |

**Source**: [AI Gateway - Policy-Driven Model Routing - Engineering Overview](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/7001278725)

