## 6. Fallback & Circuit Breaker Patterns

### 6.1 Current Fallback Mappings

| Primary Model | Fallback Model |
|--------------|----------------|
| OpenAI Chat Completion models | gemini-2.5-flash |
| Bedrock Anthropic Claude models | Google Anthropic Claude models |
| Google Anthropic Claude models | Bedrock Anthropic Claude models |
| Gemini 3 Flash | gemini-2.5-flash |

### 6.2 Fallback Strategy Header

```
X-Atlassian-Fallback-Strategy: ENFORCED | DEFAULT | NONE | SLO
```

- `ENFORCED`: Forces routing to fallback model (useful for testing)
- `DEFAULT`: Automatic platform fallback on failure
- `NONE`: No fallback, consumer handles own retry
- `SLO`: (New) Multi-hop fallback using SLO registry chain

### 6.3 Circuit Breaker Configuration

- **Per-instance, per use-case, per model**
- Opens when failure rate exceeds threshold (5% of requests, minimum 20 calls in 60 seconds)
- States: CLOSED → OPEN → HALF-OPEN
- **Automated fallback enabled by default** for all use cases
- Plan to move to distributed (Redis-backed) circuit breaker for global protection

### 6.4 Internal-Only (AHL/AHM) CloudID Routing

For organizations with `atlassianHostedLLMs = true`:
1. External LLM Validator blocks external routes
2. Automatic fallback to TeamServe (GPT-OSS models)
3. Fallback strategies: `DEFAULT`, `LLAMA_70B`, `GPT_OSS_20B_TS`, `GPT_OSS_120B_TS`, `ENFORCED` (→ Gemini)

**Source**: [AI Gateway Platform Fallback](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/5796071618), [Deep Dive: AI gateway Fallback pattern](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6457728982)

---

## 7. Rate Limiting

### 7.1 How It Works

AI Gateway uses **Heimdall** (via Hofund sidecar) for rate limiting:
- **Cost-based rate limiting** (default) — calls Heimdall twice per request: once with estimated cost (pre-request), once with actual cost (post-response)
- Default: **100k TPM (Tokens Per Minute)** per use case per model
- Keys: `client` (ASAP issuer), `tenant` (model ID), `user` (user ID), `ip` (model-ID for TPM), `artifact` (use-case-ID)

### 7.2 Rate Limit Management (CLI)

```bash
atlas ml aigateway usecase ratelimit view -i <use_case_id> -e <environment> -m <model_id>
```

### 7.3 Response Headers on Rate Limit

| Header | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `X-RateLimit-Limit` | Max TPM for use case/model |
| `X-RateLimit-Type` | `MODEL.USE_CASE`, `USER`, `USE_CASE.MODEL.TENANT`, `UPSTREAM` |
| `Retry-After` | Seconds to wait |
| `X-RateLimit-Reset` | Timestamp of limit reset |

**Source**: [AI Gateway Rate Limits](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/6152697444), [AI Gateway Heimdall Decisions](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~70121059708b83b364a50bb46c0251ea64a04/pages/6484558143)

