## 9. SDK Options

### 9.1 AI Gateway SDK (Official — Java, Python, Node.js)

**Maven/Gradle** (Java):
```xml
<dependency><groupId>com.atlassian.mlp</groupId>
    <artifactId>ai-gateway-sdk</artifactId>
    <version>LATEST_VERSION</version>
</dependency>
```

**Three client modes** (SDK V7):
1. **Typed Client** — Full contract validation, generated DTOs, compile-time safety
2. **Generic Client** — Auth/routing wired, flexible request/response (no strict validation)
3. **Raw Client** — Direct HTTP, no contract validation, full JSON control

**Java example** (Typed):
```java
OpenAI openaiClient = AIGatewayClient.sync()
    .defaultHeader(AIGatewayHeaders.USE_CASE_ID, "your-use-case-id")
    .defaultHeader(AIGatewayHeaders.CLOUD_ID, "your-cloud-id")
    .defaultHeader(AIGatewayHeaders.USER_ID, "your-user-id")
    .build()
    .openai();
```

### 9.2 Go Client (Anti-Abuse maintained)

```go
import "bitbucket.org/antiabuse/commons/aigateway"

client, err := aigateway.NewClient(ctx)
req := &aigateway.UnifiedChatRequest{
    PlatformAttributes: aigateway.RequestPlatformAttributes{
        Model: "claude-opus-4-1@20250805",
    },
    RequestPayload: aigateway.RequestPayload{
        Messages: []aigateway.Message{...},
        MaxCompletionTokens: func() *int32 { v := int32(512); return &v }(),
    },
}
resp, err := client.Chat(ctx, req)
```

### 9.3 Python SDK

Available via `pip install ai-gateway-sdk`. Auth via ASAP or SLAuth. Same three client modes.

**Source**: [Announcing AI Gateway SDK v7](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/blog/2026/01/27/6365279255), [AI Integrations & SDKs](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ATF/pages/6976383021)

