    wrapping an httpx.Client(limits=, timeout=). State emitted as a metric
    every call. Constructor-injectable for tests.
  2 Resilient pipeline (fail-open kill-switch) —
    src/refactored/inference_models/resilient_pipeline.py (174 lines):
    ResilientPipeline(Moderator) decorator that catches a closed exception
    hierarchy (ModelTimeoutError, ModelCircuitBreakerOpen,
    MalformedModelOutput, ModelTransportError, AIGatewayError) and consults
    feature_service.should_fail_open_*() at call time to either fail-open
    ALLOWED or raise APIException.
  3 Shadow / A-B pipeline — src/refactored/inference_models/shadower.py:
    ShadowedPipeline(primary, shadow, evaluator) runs shadow via gevent.spawn
    in a bounded Pool(20) with contextvars.copy_context(). Composable with
    ResilientPipeline. Canonical pattern for rovo-eval-runner /
    aix-eval-runner.
  4 Backend ABC / shared ML client base —
    src/refactored/inference_models/backends/base.py: ModerationBackend ABC,
    ResponseParser ABC, BackendResponse / ParsedOutput dataclasses, plus
    _translate_transport_error() that normalises
    pybreaker.CircuitBreakerError, httpx.TimeoutException,
    httpx.TransportError, requests.Timeout, Triton
    InferenceServerException("Deadline Exceeded"), AIGatewayResponseException
    → unified hierarchy. Backends: ai_gateway.py, sagemaker.py, teamserve.py.
  5 SageMaker auth pattern — src/inference_models/sagemaker_base.py:
    SageMakerInferenceBase(ABC) with boto3.Session() default → STS
    AssumeRole(SageMakerExecutionRole) fallback. Hard-coded role ARN noted as
    a gap.
  6 SLAuth / ASAP — policies/service/ + nebulae.yml (slauth plugin, asapKey: 
    service, egressEnv: stg-east) for internal service-to-service auth.
  7 Feature gates / kill-switches — src/feature_service.py with 3-tier
    override priority (per-request debug.feature_overrides → local file →
    Statsig). Features StrEnum with inline
    owner/type/created/cleanup-by/switcheroo-gotcha metadata.
    src/dynamic_config/client.py wraps StatsigSidecarClient.
  8 Detectors-as-code (gold standard) — operations/terraform/detectors.tf (207
    lines, 5 detectors). Pattern: locals.opsgenie_team_id + locals.runbook_url
    + locals.critical_notifications shared; each signalfx_detector mirrors a
    dashboard.tf chart 1-for-1, links a runbook URL, tags the Jira ticket, and
    carries inline rationale citing the canonical incident. Repo had 17 charts
    / 0 detectors before this file — ml-launch-review-checklist should encode
    "charts without detectors is a smell".
  9 Canary / progressive deploy — default-pipelines.spinnaker.yaml
    (progressiveRollout: useDefault: true at stg-east) +
    helm/templates/webserver.yaml + archetype-descriptor.yaml + nebulae.yml
    form the deploy-manifest set.
