## Finding 6: Model Validation Gates (Production Readiness)

### What it is
A three-level verification framework that models must pass before production deployment. Launchpad provides the tooling for Levels 1 and 2 via ML Studio workflow modules.

### How it works

**Level 1: Functional Correctness (Launch Validation)**
- Module: `ts_lp_launch_validation`
- Validates: model boots, accepts requests, returns expected output
- Parameters:
  - `component_ref` (STRING) — ML Registry component
  - `version_ref` (INT) — Version ID
  - `golden_request` (STRING/JSON) — Known-good input payload
  - `load_model` (STRING) — Triton model name
  - `instance_type` (STRING) — GPU type
  - `time_to_live_minutes` (INT, default 60)
  - `max_wait_minutes` (INT, default 15)

- Phases checked: `launch` → `readiness` → `inference` → `contract`
- Output annotation type: `ts_launch_validation` (written to ML Registry version)- Pass/fail status
  - Cold start time (seconds)
  - Readiness poll count
  - Golden response latency (ms)
  - Response shape summary
  - Full launch config

**Level 2: Performance & Scalability (Load Test Validation)**
- Module: `ts_lp_loadtest_validation`
- Parameters:
  - `component_ref`, `version_ref` (required)
  - `payload_data` (STRING/JSON) — Request bodies for perf_analyzer
  - `instance_types` (STRING/JSON) — Array of EC2 types to test
  - `job_args` (STRING/JSON) — perf_analyzer flags (e.g., `{"measurement-request-count": 10, "request-rate-range": "1:60:5"}`)
  - `container_args` (STRING/JSON) — Must include `loadModel`
  - `loadtest_job_id` (STRING, auto:12-char hex)
  - `time_to_live_minutes` (INT, default 60)
  - `max_wait_minutes` (INT, default 30)

**Level 3: Quality & Baseline Comparison**
- Owned by model owners (not yet automated via Launchpad)
- Validates model delivers better results than existing baseline

**ML Studio Workflow YAML (Gate Chain):**
```yaml
module_tasks:
  - step_name: validate_ts_launchpad
    module: ts_lp_launch_validation
    version: :latestAlpha
    parameters:
      - name: component_ref
        value: "your-namespace.your-component"
      - name: version_ref
        value:42
      - name: golden_request
        value: '{"inputs":[...]}'
      - name: load_model
        value: "your_triton_model_name"
      - name: instance_type
        value: "g6e.xlarge"

  - step_name: run_ts_launchpad_loadtest
    module: ts_lp_loadtest_validation
    version: :latestAlpha
    depends_on:
      - validate_ts_launchpad
    parameters:
      - name: component_ref
        value: "your-namespace.your-component"
      - name: version_ref
        value: 42
      ...
```

**Workflow CLI Commands:**
```bash
# Validate workflow
atlas ml workflow validate -d workflows/src/<team>/my_validation_workflow.yaml --env staging

# Submit workflow blueprint
atlas ml workflow submit -d workflows/src/<team>/my_validation_workflow.yaml -e prod

# Run workflow
atlas ml workflow run -b<blueprint-id> -e prod
```

### How it applies
The skill should implement a gate-checking workflow:
1. `launch_validation` gate — must pass before load testing
2. `loadtest_validation` gate — must pass before production readiness
3. Both gates annotate results to ML Registry for audit trail
4. Human confirmation required before production promotion (not self-service)

### Source
- [ML Studio Modules for Launchpad Model Validation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120203e8fad871e7f452c8bec69de58960c46/pages/6750537331)
- [Design Doc: ts_lp_launch_validation & ts_lp_loadtest_validation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120203e8fad871e7f452c8bec69de58960c46/pages/6962155706)
- [Validate Your Model with TeamServe Launchpad](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020a570c71e24c846068af97060212d4544/pages/6986170999)
- [Levels of Model Quality and Platform Verification](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AO2/pages/6432265318)

