## Finding 9: Rate Limits and Known Limitations

### What it is
Launchpad has both API-level and infrastructure-level constraints.

### How it works

**API Gateway Limits (SageMaker path):**
- 29-second timeout on API Gateway (AWS-imposed, account-level)
- Lambda: 6MB invocation payload (request and response)
- Lambda: 50concurrent executions (default, can be raised)
- Lambda: 15-minute timeout

**Workaround for long invokes:**
- FastAPI service (`POST /v2/model_group/model_version`) bypasses API Gateway limits
- Direct SageMaker invocation eliminates one network hop
- Supports response streaming (SSE)

**TEAMServe path (newer):**
- No API Gateway limitation (direct to FastAPI/Micros)
- Timeout controlled by the FastAPI service configuration
- ASAP auth token expiry applies

**Infrastructure limits:**
- Single replica per deployment (no auto-scaling)
- Limited GPU instance options: `g6e.xlarge`, `g5.2xlarge`
- TTL default: 2 hours (configurable via `expiry_time_epoch`)
- No UGC data on non-compliant models (enforced via policy)
- One model per endpoint in Launchpad

### How it applies
The skill should include retry logic for timeout scenarios and document the payload size limitations for the SageMaker path. For TEAMServe path, the primary constraint is cold-start time (model download + Triton loading).

### Source
- [RFC: Handling Long Invokes in Launchpad](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/4982837961)
- [Launchpad Lambda and API Gateway Limitations](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/3957251871)

