## Finding 10: Load Testing API

### What it is
Launchpad provides integrated load testing via perf_analyzer (NVIDIA's tool for Triton) through both the SDK and ML Studio modules.

### How it works

**SDK-based Load Test:**
```python
ep = launchpad.launch_to_teamserve(...)
loadtest = ep.run_load_test(
    job_id="my-test-01",
    input_data=[payload_data],
    job_args={
        "measurement-request-count": 10,
        "request-rate-range": "1:60:5",
        "measurement-mode": "count_windows"
    },
    model_name="my_model"
)
```

**API-based Load Test (SageMaker path):**
```
POST /models/<model_group>/<model_version>/load-test

Body:
{
    "sample_payload_uri": "s3://...",
    "model_group_name": "msp-sample-models",
    "model_version_tag": "v1",
    "instance_types": ["ml.g5xlarge"],
    "traffic_patterns": [{
        "initial_num_users": 1,
        "spawn_rate": 1,
        "duration": 1200
    }]
}

Response:
{
    "test_run": "<url>",
    "job_name": "adsf-1234"
}
```

**Job Naming Convention:** `<model-hash>-lt-<JOBID>`

### How it applies
Load testing is a gate in the production readiness workflow. The tool should expose load test triggering and results retrieval. Results include p50/p90/p99 latency at various request rates per instance type.

### Source
- [Load Testing on TEAMServe Launchpad](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/blog/2026/03/26/6714832386)
- [API Design for Load Test Capability](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/3821642124)

