## Finding 2: Endpoint Status Lifecycle and State Machine

### What it is
Launchpad manages deployment status through a defined state machine that drives the system's behavior (whether to deploy, poll, invoke, or return errors).

### How it works

```python
class EndpointStatus(Enum):
    NOT_EXIST = "NotExist"
    IN_SERVICE = "InService"
    CREATING = "Creating"
    ROLLING_BACK = "RollingBack"
    UPDATING = "Updating"
    DELETING = "Deleting"
    FAILED = "Failed"
    UNKNOWN = "Unknown"
```

**State → Behavior mapping:**

| Status | Definition | Launchpad Behavior |
|--------|-----------|-------------------|
| InService | Ready to call | `launch`: return existing endpoint; `invoke`: call endpoint |
| Creating | Spinning up | Poll until ready |
| Failed | Deployment failed | Return message to check logs/metrics; pod stops restarting |
| Deleting | Being deleted | Tell user to wait before retrying |
| NotExist | Not deployed (deleted/expired) | Deploy on launch request |

**Deployment Creation Flow:**
```
User Request (POST /launch)
    → API Validation & Manifest Generation
    → ArgoCD Detects Change
    → ArgoCD Syncs to Data Plane
    → Node Provisioning (if needed)
    → Pod Scheduled
    → Init: deployment-store-client (fetch manifest)
    → Init: model-downloader (download model to instance)
    → Triton Server Starts & Loads Model
    → Health Checks Pass
    → Status: InService ✅
```

### How it applies
The skill should encode the polling pattern: after a `launch` call, poll `status/{id}` at15-second intervals until `InService` or `Failed` (timeout: 900 seconds). The AI must handle the transient `Unknown` state during ArgoCD sync window gracefully.

### Source
- [Status and Model Lifecycle](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5991160850)
- [Launchpad/TEAMServe Technical Design Doc](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AO2/pages/6024494365)

