## Finding 11: Enterprise Deployment Gating (EPM/EGRM)

### What it is
Separate from Launchpad's internal gates, Atlassian has an Enterprise Posture Management (EPM) deployment gating system that blocks production deployments based on compliance posture.

### How it works

**Gate Control Structure:**
```json
{
    "id": "985818eb-...",
    "component": "service",
    "instanceId": "compliance-assurance-svc",
    "gateAttributes": {
        "type": "deployment",
        "environmentTypes": "staging",
        "perimeters": "fedramp-moderate"
    },
    "status": "BLOCK",
    "blockDecisionReason": {
        "failing_responsibilities": [
            {
                "responsibility_id": "3eefe18b-...",
                "responsibility_title": "Encoding of services in the Atlassian Environment Model"
            }
        ]
    }
}
```

**Decision Logic:** ALLOW if no failing projections or an accepted exception exists; otherwise BLOCK.

**Gating Policies (Metadata Gatekeeper):**

| Policy | Dev | Staging | Prod | FedRAMP |
|--------|-----|---------|------|---------|
| `asset_readiness_release_blocker` | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |
| `artifact_compliant` | ✗ | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ |
| `artifact_signed` | ✗ | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ |
| `cloud_resource_tagging` | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | ✗ |

**Note:** Compliance is NOT required for Launchpad deployments (pre-prod only). It IS required when promoting to production TEAMServe.

### How it applies
The skill should document that Launchpad bypasses enterprise deployment gating (it's a dev/test environment), but production promotion requires passing all compliance gates. The "golden path" is: Launchpad validation → Compliance check → Production deployment via TEAMServe onboarding ticket.

### Source
- [Deployment artifact compliance](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MICROS/pages/4448556873)
- [RFC: EPM Deployment Gating](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/entcap/pages/5655014289)
- [MLP Bluebird - Launchpad scope decision](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6153124254)

