## Finding 12: Deployment Lifecycle Environments

### What it is
The ML platform defines a three-environment model for model deployment maturity.

### How it works

| Attribute | Launchpad | Experimental (new) | Prod |
|-----------|-----------|-------------------|------|
| Primary Goal | Testing/dev environment | Test in realistic serving context | Serve durable product traffic |
| Lifetime | Hours (TTL-based) | Weeks (stop/extend/graduate) | Indefinite |
| TS Environment | Dev/testing | Prod* | Prod |
| Traffic | Synthetic/manual/test | Bounded realistic (shadow, dogfood, limited A/B) | Live product traffic |
| Onboarding | Self-service | Service owners swap models | TS managed |
| Compliance | Not required | Required (customer traffic) | Required |
| Scale | 1 replica only | Limited | Scaled for needs |
| Multi-Region | 1 only | Fixed | Supported |
| SLOs | None | None | Managed |
| On-call | N/A | Experiment owner accountable | Production support applies |

### How it applies
The skill should encode which gates apply at each stage. Launchpad is the entry point (no compliance, self-service, ephemeral). Production requires all gates.

### Source
- [DRAFT - RFC: Experimental Environment in TEAMserve](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AO2/pages/7046240557)

