**What to produce**: Practical, actionable findings — concrete patterns, templates, frameworks, and best practices that can be directly used in a skill/tool specification. This is NOT an academic literature review.

**Source Guidance — Prioritize in this order:**
1. Official documentation for relevant platforms and tools mentioned in the task description
2. Industry-standard frameworks and methodologies (e.g., NIST AI RMF, ITIL, PMI, SAFe) — focus on the practical application, not theoretical foundations
3. Well-established best practices from recognized organizations — concrete templates, checklists, and workflow patterns
4. Real-world case studies with measurable outcomes

**Output Structure**: For each finding, provide:
- **What it is**: The pattern, template, framework, or best practice
- **How it works**: Concrete steps, fields, criteria, or structure
- **How it applies**: How this would be encoded in a skill (SKILL.md workflow guidance) or tool (executable operations)
- **Source**: Where you found it (URL, standard name, or organization)

**AI-Specific Considerations** — this skill/tool will be used by an AI employee:
- Focus on patterns that can be expressed as step-by-step workflows (good for SKILL.md)
- Identify where human confirmation should be required vs. autonomous execution
- Note any domain-specific terminology or taxonomies the AI needs to understand

## Original User Request
**Description**: Conduct external + cross-platform research on the actual APIs/CLIs/SDKs of the 14 named ML platforms AND the domain knowledge needed for the 7 SOP skills. Two complementary streams in one deliverable. Stream A (Platform API discovery, for tool surfaces): For each platform — MLflow (run/params/metrics/artifact logging, run-name conventions), ML Studio + Databricks + ML Fabric (training job launch, HPO sweeps Optimus Prime / Bayesian, convergence diagnostics), Tarot v3 Registry (register/query/promote, lineage + compliance metadata), MLFS / Tecton (feature read/write/audit, coverage/freshness/sparsity, online↔offline consistency), ML Lens (KS/KL/embedding-cosine drift metrics, dashboards, alert subscriptions), SignalFx (detectors-as-code, per-endpoint SLO IaC), TEAMServe (gRPC deploy/rollback/canary, Micros descriptors), SageMaker (endpoints, GPU autoscaling, AZ rotation), AI Gateway (routing config for OpenAI/Anthropic/Bedrock/Gemini/internal LLM), Launchpad (deploy launch APIs/gates), rovo-eval & AIX-eval (workflow trigger + structured results), Symphony + ORBIT (context bind read/write, RFC-002 L1–L5 autonomy policy validation) — document auth model, endpoints/CLI, request/response formats, rate limits, internal client libraries. Stream B (Domain knowledge for the 7 SOP skills): research best practices for experiment lifecycle (literature synthesis, pre-analysis registration, parallel variants, mandatory ablations, multi-seed mean±std, architecture comparison report templates), drift-triggered retraining (signal correlation, baseline reproduction, canary gating, rollback criteria), incident response (circuit-breaker patterns, cross-correlation, 30-min cadence comms, auto-PIR drafting), deployment manifest (invariants/risk/test/rollback/post-deploy monitoring schemas), launch review checklist gates (Google PAIR, Microsoft Responsible AI), runbook authoring templates/refresh cadence, evaluation rigor (every-failure-case categorization, slicing, k-fold + calibration + CIs + fairness, ablation interaction analysis).

