### 1.5 Rovo Dev Skills-Builder Eval Framework

**What it is**: A framework for generating and running evaluations of Rovo Dev CLI skills. Focuses on skill trigger accuracy and workflow execution quality.

**Source**: [How To Generate and Run AI Skill Evaluations](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020742e2e14c1da465192bd8fc1ff1a2b56/pages/6888039198)

#### Trigger CLI:
```shell
# Generate evals from skills
skills-builder generate-evals ./skills -o eval/

# Run evaluation with comparison
skills-builder compare-evals eval/existing-skill.evals.json \-w /path/to/repo -s ./skills --trials 3
```

#### Eval Dataset Schema (`.evals.json`):
```json
{
  "skill_name": "module-scaffolding-workflow",
  "evals": [
    {
      "id": "scaffold_csv_summarizer",
      "prompt": "hey, can you add a new feature to parse csv reports...",
      "expected_output": "The agent should explore the codebase...",
      "language": "python",
      "should_trigger": true,
      "expected_checks": [
        "analyzes_existing_conventions",
        "decomposes_into_multiple_files",
        "writes_unit_tests",
        "validates_with_tests"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "negative_unrelated_bug_fix",
      "prompt": "the report parser is crashing on empty input, can u fix it?",
      "expected_output": "The agent should fix the bug directly...",
      "language": "python",
      "should_trigger": false,
      "expected_checks": []
    }
  ]
}
```

