─── Response ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

No single SoR exists. GPU quota/allocation/consumption is federated across 4
surfaces, all reachable via existing MCP tools (no new MCP server needed):

 1 TEAMServe (inference) — AWS ODCRs in account 359877971362 shared via RAM
   shared-reservation-team-serve to KITT account 850995561789. Read via aws 
   ec2 describe-capacity-reservations --filters 
   Name=tag:service_name,Values=teamserve after atlas cloudtoken; live
   allocation via kubectl get nodeclaim. Runbooks: AO2/5447899830 (read),
   AO2/5545208530 (write), tracker AO2/5043553305.
 2 SageMaker (legacy) — Truman-Prod-User / Truman-EU-Prod-User accounts;
   quotas via AWS Service Quotas API; live view via SignalFx dashboard
   GG671nHA0AM; intake via go/mldesk → AWS Support. Pages MLP/3402975183,
   MLP/6527920973.
 3 GCP — Centralized in a FinOps-owned GCP project, shared to consumers;
   tracker at MLP/6144859415; intake CFINOPS/6152685071. Example:
   reservation-aiserving-a3ultra (4×a3-ultra, us-central1-b).
 4 Training (Kueue/GKE) — Cohort-level quotas (e.g., H200 Cohort = 32 GPUs
   split across Critical-Short/Critical-Long/Experimental ClusterQueues),
   reservation-first admission with DWS flex fallback. Page MLP/6649766642.

Cost attribution SoR = Databricks table
production.cloud_finops_ias.ai_cost_daily_summary (columns: provider,
usage_date, cost_center, service_group, service_name, product, model_name,
effective_cost). Reachable today via mcp__socrates; future REST API in flight
in finops-service (CFINOPS/7045396956). FY26-Q4 top spenders: content_index
$965K (24%), tecton $372K, ml_platform $365K, teamserve $315K, idle_capacity
$53K.

Scale-down hooks:

 • Serving: Karpenter consolidation + HPA + AWS modify-capacity-reservation;
   Tecton uses scheduled kubectl scale via Bitbucket Pipelines + OIDC +
   atlassian/aws-eks-kubectl-run:2.7.0 pipe (DACI MLP/6409031846 picked
   weekend time-based scale-down).
 • Training: No centralized convergence-detection / early-stop API exists.
   Available levers = Kueue preemption, MLflow set_terminated(run_id, 
   "KILLED"), ML Studio MSP SDK cancel. → SKILL should emit recommendations
   gated to 🟡/🔴 human sign-off.

Cost-attribution rule (critical for SKILL): idle reserved capacity → charged
to ML Platform team; consumed capacity → charged to owning service. Idle
right-sizing runbook MLP/6567768725 (rule of thumb: cap idle at 5 instances,
target = historical low).

Coverage matrix verdict: A gpu-quota-tracker should be implemented as a thin 
aggregator SKILL composing mcp__socrates + mcp__compass + mcp__atlassian +
mcp__bitbucket + bash. Join key: service_name tag on ODCR ↔ service_name
column in cost table ↔ service_uuid in Compass.

Gaps:

 • No MCP wrapper for AWS CLI/kubectl (use bash).
 • No MCP for MLflow / ML Studio job cancel.
 • Manual capacity tracker page editing.
 • §5.3 $5.6M / 59% savings figure not directly grounded in any single
   Confluence page — closest evidence in MLP/5965061506 (idle reservations
   analysis) and SRCA/4785377572. Aggregator should either mark as
   illustrative or do a follow-up post-mortem search.
 • No dedicated 🟡/🔴 escalation playbook page — SKILL must define thresholds
   from role §10.5.


