     Key findings (runbooks / 🟡🔴 escalation playbooks / ROI templates)

1. There IS a fully-formed governance system for the 🔴 large-delta tier — the
AI Cost Council in the dedicated Central-AI-Cost Confluence space:

 • Charter page 6637208927 (governance scope: capacity demand approval,
   model-mix changes, alignment with L1/L2 AI OKRs)
 • Approval Request Template page 6714530711 — 14-field schema (Title /
   Description / Sponsor / Type of cost / DRI / Functional grouping /
   Customers / Cost forecast / Where cost lands / Value / Request ticket /
   Approver / Status / Approved spend)
 • Open Cost Requests kanban (6707848246), Decision Register audit log
   (6721895129), Backlog (6765722332), and biweekly ACC meeting agendas (Apr
   1/Apr 8/Apr 21/May 12/May 26 — 30 min: 3 intro + 8 per topic + 3 summary,
   organized by Hendrik Thomas & Deepankar Dubey)
 • Two filled examples: rate-limit raise +$30K/mo (7063670922), Jira Semantic
   Search (7034582084)

2. There is NO single 🟡/🔴 color-coded doc — the role's color tiers are
SKILL-internal. The SKILL must own threshold definitions (recommended:
🔴≥$30K/mo OR model-mix change for LLM; 🟡 below). The de-facto 🟡 venue is
#ai-economics Slack + the AI cost mgmt Weekly planning page (7049952494).

3. Budget-reallocation runbook is a PLACEHOLDER — ML Studio Cost Transfer
(7050593207) page body is literally <p></p>. Only scaffolding is RFC
7050535235 (driver Apoorva Uday Nayak; due 2026-05-31) which defines the
cost-ownership taxonomy but not the transfer mechanics. Gap: SKILL must draft
the workflow on top of the RFC's taxonomy and notify drivers.

4. No org-wide ROI template — but a strong de-facto pattern across:

 • Bluebird per-model ROI (6527257073, "50-60% cost reductions") — {model, 
   env, replicas, instance, $/mo} before/after schema
 • TeamServe Impact (7071594260) — narrative wins (Launchpad, load-testing
   4h→<20min, g7e2xlarge 42% latency)
 • Cost Savings tracker (7080719266) — authoritative per-model rollup
 • ML Studio NAT Gateway $5.5M doc (6359646748) — likely source of the
   role-doc "$5.6M/yr" figure (list price $5.5M, effective $1.75M, joint
   MLP×Plato×FinOps×Cloud-Networking attribution)
 • ML Studio Cost Reduction ERD (6400346399), MOI Gaps for Non-LLM Cost
   (7083638717), AI Cost: Finance vs Production Comparison (7034359277),
   Master Migration Guide (7081364303), QI Migration Plan (7073104504)

5. GPU sign-off runbooks — GPU Capacity Planning (6894656228, "ping @Rekha
Ganesh ≥4 wk before"), TEAMServe GPU Capacity Management (5425146514, P0
metrics: cost-per-call, model breakdown, active/unused), TS: GPU allocations
(6944169914), AWS SageMaker Service Quota (3402975183), plus parallel FinOps
GCP Capacity Reservations DACI cadence (7075074794/7068718932/7052246143,
driven by Shreya Ambast / approver Sara Gadallah or Tom Cutajar).

                    Recommendations for the SKILL designer

 • Unified ROI schema proposed in §4.2 of the report — superset of Bluebird +
   ML Studio ERD + MOI Gaps formats.
 • 🔴 workflow is fully composable today (template → file Jira → crosslink
   next ACC → append Decision Register).
 • 🟡 workflow must be synthesized (Slack + weekly page row + Cost
   Optimization Log append).
 • Budget transfer is the largest gap — SKILL provides a pre-draft, but
   ultimate mechanism awaits RFC 7050535235 completion.
 • Threshold defaults & Jira project (CTSC vs MLP) should be SKILL config
   keys.
 • ACC cadence is biweekly in practice — poll for next existing ACC page
   rather than assume fixed weekday.


