## 5. End-to-End Drift-Triggered Retraining Workflow

### 5.1 Complete Workflow Template

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ PHASE 1: MONITORING (Autonomous)                            │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ML Lens computes drift metrics every ~5 min│
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Alert engine evaluates thresholds (PSI > 0.2, KS p< 0.05) │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Signal correlation: multiple features drifting?│
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Model performance also degrading?                           │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ If YES to both → emit retraining event to StreamHub         │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ PHASE 2: RETRAINING (Autonomous with gates)                 │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ML Studio Orchestrator consumes event       │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Check cooldown (last retrain > 24h ago?)                    │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Reproduce baseline model (same config, original data)       │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Train candidate on updated data                             │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Step 1: Evaluate candidate vs baseline (offline metrics)    │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ GATE: Candidate must MATCH OR EXCEED baseline               │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Step 2: Package candidate, re-evaluate vs baseline          │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Register candidate in ML Registry as "challenger"           │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ PHASE 3: DEPLOYMENT (Human-gated)                           │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 🔒 HUMAN APPROVAL: Review candidate metrics│
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Deploy to shadow (same traffic, offline evaluation)         │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Shadow soak: 1-7 days, compare outputs                      │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ GATE: Shadow metrics acceptable?                            │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Deploy canary (10% traffic)                                 │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Canary soak: 24h minimum                    │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Automated canary analysis (SignalFx detectors)              │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ GATE: Pass/fail based on severity-tiered criteria│
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Progressive ramp: 10% → 50% → 100%                         │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Promote challenger to "champion" alias                      │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ PHASE 4: POST-DEPLOYMENT (Autonomous with kill-switch)      │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Continuous monitoring (same drift + performance metrics)     │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Circuit breaker protection on inference endpoint            │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ If CB trips OR accuracy drops → auto-rollback               │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Update ML Registry: demote challenger, restore champion     │
│ ↓                                                           │
│ Disable automatic retraining until investigated│
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 5.2 Human Confirmation Points (L1-L5Autonomy Mapping)

| Step | Autonomy Level | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| Drift detection | L4 (Autonomous) | Statistical computation, no risk |
| Retraining trigger | L3 (Autonomous + notify) | Notify owner, proceed unless vetoed |
| Model training | L4 (Autonomous) | Compute-only, no production impact |
| Offline evaluation | L4 (Autonomous) | Read-only comparison |
| Shadow deployment | L2 (Recommend, human confirms) | First production-adjacent step |
| Canary deployment | L2 (Recommend, human confirms) | Live traffic affected |
| Auto-rollback on CRITICAL | L4 (Autonomous) | Time-critical safety action |
| Investigation after rollback | L1 (Human-driven) | Root cause requires judgment |

