## Synthesis: How These Apply to an ML Incident Response Skill

### Workflow Encoding for SKILL.md

```
ML_INCIDENT_RESPONSE_WORKFLOW:

Phase 1 — DETECT (autonomous)1. Alert fires (SignalFx detector, Pollinator synthetic, or manual report)
  2. Cross-correlate with related alerts (check correlation graph)
  3. Check circuit breaker states on affected endpoints
  4. Classify severity using TTD/impact mapping
  5. Auto-create HOT ticket if threshold met

Phase 2 — RESPOND (autonomous + human confirmation)
  6. Post initial declaration in #incidents (5-min SLA)
  7. Activate kill-switch if blast radius > threshold [HUMAN CONFIRM]
  8. Enable fail-open if model endpoint is degraded [autonomous if gate exists]
  9. Start30-min communication cadence timer
  10. Page relevant teams based on faulty service mapping

Phase 3 — INVESTIGATE (autonomous analysis + human decision)
  11. Cross-correlate signals (model latency, GPU util, upstream status)
  12. Check recent deployments and config changes
  13. Identify root cause hypothesis
  14. Post investigation update every 15-30 min (even "no change")

Phase 4 — MITIGATE (human-confirmed actions)
  15. Execute remediation (rollback, scale-up, config revert) [HUMAN CONFIRM]
  16. Verify metrics improving
  17. Post "cause identified" + "fix in progress" updates
  18. Verify resolution across all regions/tenants

Phase 5 — CLOSE & LEARN (autonomous draft + human review)
  19. Post resolution confirmation
  20. Auto-generate PIR from Slack + ticket + monitoring data
  21. Populate all mandatory sections with AI-draft markers
  22. Flag sections needing human validation
  23. Create follow-up action items as Jira tickets
  24. Schedule PIR review meeting
```

### Human Confirmation Points (RFC-002L1-L5 mapping)

| Action | Autonomy Level | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| Post status update (factual) | L4 (autonomous with log) | Template-driven, low risk |
| Enable fail-open gate | L3 (auto with human notification) | Pre-approved safe default |
| Activate kill-switch | L2 (propose, human confirms) | Customer-impacting |
| Rollback deployment | L2 (propose, human confirms) | Service state change |
| Generate PIR draft | L4 (autonomous with log) | Draft only, requires review |
| Approve PIR | L1 (human-only) | Organizational accountability |

### Domain Taxonomy the AI Must Understand

- **TTD** (Time to Detect): Alert fire → human acknowledges
- **TTH** (Time to Handle): Alert → incident manager engaged
- **TTR** (Time to Resolve): Impact start → customer impact ends
- **TTC** (Time to Communicate): Declaration → first external update
- **Fail-open**: Service returns ALLOWED/pass-through when model is unavailable
- **Fail-closed**: Service blocks all requests when model is unavailable
- **Kill-switch**: Runtime control to completely halt traffic to a service/model/region
- **Circuit breaker states**: Closed (normal) → Open (blocking) → Half-Open (probing)
- **Blast radius**: Scope of customer/service impact from a failure
- **Error budget**: SLO allowance for failures before requiring action[0m
