## Original User Request
**Description**: Design and create the Cost, Capacity & FinOps stewardship skill and tool set for the AI MLE. Drivers: §2 R10, §4.3 (FinOps dashboards, ML Artifact Cost Monitoring), §5.3 (SageMaker→TEAMServe ~$5.6M/yr migration exemplar), §9 (cost-attribution challenges), §10.5 (GPU budget sign-off escalation), §11.1 (GPU quota).

Proposed SKILL:
  • `ml-cost-stewardship` — Workflow for continuous cost monitoring, anomaly detection (cost-vs-historical-median), per-experiment budget enforcement, auto scale-down on convergence, and infra-migration ROI analysis (e.g., SageMaker→TEAMServe ~59% savings pattern). Includes escalation logic for 🟡 budget reallocation and 🔴 large-delta sign-off. Generates recommendation reports.

Proposed TOOLS (only if not covered by existing tools per subtask 1):
  • `ml-cost-query` — Query inference cost/request, GPU utilization, training cost per model version from FinOps dashboards and ML Artifact Cost Monitoring; slice by model program / endpoint / region.
  • `gpu-quota-tracker` — Read current GPU allocation and consumption vs. quota; trigger scale-down on convergence; flag anomalies.
  • `infra-migration-analyzer` — Project cost deltas for migrations (e.g., SageMaker→TEAMServe), producing structured comparison reports with assumptions, sensitivity, and recommended action.

Why separate from subtask 2: Cost/FinOps uses different data sources (FinOps systems, Artifact Cost Monitoring) and is a recommendation/reporting surface rather than a control-plane action. Keeping it isolated preserves a clear responsibility boundary and avoids bloating the platform-core tools.

Research requirement: Discover the actual FinOps dashboard APIs, ML Artifact Cost Monitoring endpoints, and any internal cost-attribution services. Confirm whether the existing `s360` MCP toolset or any other available tool already exposes the needed cost queries before creating new tools.

**Todos**:
- Investigate FinOps dashboard APIs and ML Artifact Cost Monitoring data sources used at Atlassian.
- Verify (against subtask 1's coverage matrix) whether s360 or any other existing tool exposes per-model / per-endpoint cost data.
- Design the `ml-cost-query`, `gpu-quota-tracker`, and `infra-migration-analyzer` tool surfaces; share a common cost-data client where possible.
- Draft SKILL.md for `ml-cost-stewardship` with autonomy-tier rules (🟢 recommend, 🟡 reallocate, 🔴 large-delta) and the SageMaker→TEAMServe exemplar as a worked example.
- Define structured output schema for infra-migration ROI reports (assumptions, projected savings, risk, rollback).
</UserRequest>

