## Finding 5: TEAMServe Deployment Workflow (Exit-Criteria-Driven Stages)

### What it is
A6-phase model deployment workflow where each phase has explicit, measurable exit criteria that must be met before proceeding.

### How it works
From "How To: Deploy ML Models to TEAMServe":

```
Phase 1: Model Development & Packaging
  Exit Criteria:
    - Package builds successfully
    - Model package available in AI model registry

Phase 2: Unit Test
  Exit Criteria:
    - Model logic is correct
    - Model latency within KR (key result)
    - Model inference API is correctMethod: Launchpad

Phase 3: Validate Deployment Setup
  Exit Criteria:
    - Model artifact deployed from ML Registry to TeamServe endpoint
    - TeamServe endpoint is running
    - Model passes initialization health check
    - Searcher authorized for endpoint- Searcher deployed with correct configMethod: QD, Scraper

Phase 4: Integration Validation
  Exit Criteria:
    - Model scores match expected on test set
    - End-to-end latency within KR
  Method: Scraper, Autoscraper, Perfhammer

Phase 5: Experimentation
  Gate Conditions:
    - Experimentation capacity available
    - Pause if SLO breach (reliability, latency)Method: Monitor metrics

Phase 6: Production Launch
  Gate Conditions:
    - Model pre-launch checklist FILLED
    - Production capacity available
```

### How it applies
This provides the test_plan section's structure — a phased approach with explicit gates:

```yaml
test_plan:
  phases:
    - name: unit_validation
      method: launchpad
      exit_criteria:
        - model_logic_correct: true
        - latency_within_kr: true
        - api_contract_valid: true
    - name: integration_validation
      method: [scraper, perfhammer]
      exit_criteria:
        - scores_match_expected: threshold_0.95
        - e2e_latency_p99: <=200ms
    - name: canary_experiment
      method: statsig_experiment
      gate_conditions:
        - capacity_available: true
        - slo_breach: falserollback_trigger: slo_breach
```

### Source
- [How To: Deploy ML Models to TEAMServe](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120204aa07fe7450f489899b60900ad6a0967/pages/5959589965/How+To+Deploy+ML+Models+to+TEAMServe)
- [[RFC]TeamServe Readiness Criteria for Search at Scale](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRCA/pages/5906210553/RFC+TeamServe+Readiness+Criteria+for+Search+at+Scale)

---

## Finding 6: Rollback Schema & Safety Classification

### What it is
A structured approach to rollback safety that classifies deployments as safe or unsafe to auto-rollback, with explicit conditions for each path.

### How it works
From Atlassian's "LDR: Automatic Deployment Rollback in Production" and "RFC: Auto Rollback for Loom":

**PR-level rollback safety tagging**:
```
PR title format:
[(low/medium/high)-risk] [service-name] [not-safe-to-rollback] TICKET: Description
```

**Rollback classification**:
```yaml
rollback:
  safe_to_rollback: true | false
  classification_reason: |
    - Schema migration (irreversible state change)
    - Data format change (backward-incompatible)
    - Feature gate removal (tenants already processed under new path)
  strategy:
    if_safe:
      method: pointer_revert  # instant reversion to last-known-good
      trigger: auto_on_canary_failure
      time_to_rollback: <60s
    if_not_safe:
      method: fix_forward
      escalation: page_oncall
      manual_intervention_required: true
      alternative_mitigation: "Disable feature flag X"
```

**Auto-rollback triggers** (from RFC Auto Rollback for Loom):
- Sync failure (manifest couldn't apply)
- Verification failure (post-deploy metrics fail)
- Canary analysis failure (statistical comparison shows regression)

**Post-rollback actions**:
- Deploy thread notifies users to take action
- Automatically generate rollback shipment promoting previous image
- Leave deploys LOCKED until user intervention
- Metrics tracked: number of auto-rollbacks, time from rollback to unlock, remediation action taken

### How it applies
For ML deployments, rollback is particularly complex due to model state:

```yaml
rollback:
  safe_to_rollback: true
  fallback_model:
    name: "model-v2.3"
    registry_uri: "tarot://models/search-l2/v2.3"
    last_validated: "2026-05-20T10:00:00Z"
  auto_triggers:
    - metric: error_rate
      threshold: ">0.1%"
      sustained_duration: 5m
    - metric: p99_latency
      threshold: ">2x_baseline"
      sustained_duration: 3m
    - metric: drift_score
      threshold: ">0.1"
      sustained_duration: 15m
  manual_triggers:
    - slo_breach_detected
    - quality_degradation_reportedpost_rollback:
    - lock_deployments: true
    - notify_channel: "#ml-oncall"
    - create_incident_if: sev2_or_higher
```

### Source
- [LDR: Automatic Deployment Rollback in Production](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENCRYPT/pages/4732457812/LDR+Automatic+Deployment+Rollback+in+Production)
- [RFC: Auto Rollback for Loom](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/loomhq/pages/6594018808/RFC+Auto+Rollback+for+Loom)

---

## Finding 7: Post-Deployment Monitoring Schema

### What it is
A structured specification for what must be monitored after an ML model deployment, including health sources, verification methods, and alert configurations.

### How it works
From multiple Atlassian sources including Safe Release, Harness PDV, and ML Lens:

**Atlassian Standard Requirements** (from "Standard - Safe & Reliable Code Rollouts"):
1. **R2**: All production deployments must utilize Post Deployment Verification (PDV) including:
   - Pollinator PDV Checks (Synthetics & Health/Deep checks)
   - Canary Analysis (statistical comparison of canary vs baseline)

**Post-deploy monitoring dimensions** for ML:

```yaml
post_deploy_monitoring:
  health_checks:
    - type: liveness
      endpoint: /healthcheck
      interval: 10s
      failure_threshold: 3
    - type: readiness
      endpoint: /deepcheck
      interval: 30s
      dependencies: [model_loaded, feature_store_connected]
    - type: inference_smoke
      endpoint: /v1/predict
      test_payload: "synthetic_golden_input"
      expected_output_schema: trueinterval: 60smetrics:
    latency:
      - p50, p90, p95, p99
      - per_endpoint_breakdown: true
      - baseline_comparison: <=1.1x
    throughput:
      - requests_per_second
      - tokens_per_second (for LLMs)
    errors:
      - error_rate_total
      - error_rate_by_type: [timeout, oom, model_error, input_validation]
      - circuit_breaker_state
    resources:
      - gpu_utilization
      - gpu_memory
      - cpu_utilization
      - memory_utilization
      - disk_utilization
    model_quality:
      - drift_score (KS/KL/cosine)
      - prediction_distribution_shift
      - feature_coverage- feature_freshness

  alerts:
    - name: high_error_rate
      condition: "error_rate > 0.1% for5m"
      severity: P1
      action: auto_rollback
    - name: latency_degradation
      condition: "p99> 2x baseline for 3m"
      severity: P2
      action: page_oncall
    - name: model_drift_detected
      condition: "drift_score > 0.05 for 1h"
      severity: P3
      action: create_retraining_ticket
    - name: gpu_saturation
      condition: "gpu_util > 90% for 10m"
      severity: P2
      action: scale_out

  verification_windows:
    canary: 2h
    regional_soak: 6h
    full_production: 24h
    
  dashboards:
    primary: "signalfx://ml-models/{model_name}"
    secondary: "ml-lens://models/{model_id}/drift"
    inference: "splunk://search index=ml_inference model={model_name}"
```

### How it applies
The post-deploy monitoring section forms a critical part of the deployment manifest — it must be specified BEFORE deployment and validated during the soak period.

### Source
- [Standard - Safe & Reliable Code Rollouts](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PMP/pages/6347889982/Standard+-+Safe+Reliable+Code+Rollouts)
- [PRD: Pre and Post deployment check](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~698094961/pages/7042666133/PRD+Pre+and+Post+deployment+check)
- [Platformized ML Observability - ML Lens: One Pager](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5362077533/Platformized+ML+Observability+-+ML+Lens+One+Pager)
- [Tier 1 - Post Deployment Verification](https://home.atlassian.com/o/2346a038-3c8c-498b-a79b-e7847859868d/s/a436116f-02ce-4520-8fbb-7301462a1674/goal/ATLAS-122260)

