## Finding 5: TEAMServe Deployment Workflow (Exit-Criteria-Driven Stages)

### What it is
A6-phase model deployment workflow where each phase has explicit, measurable exit criteria that must be met before proceeding.

### How it works
From "How To: Deploy ML Models to TEAMServe":

```
Phase 1: Model Development & Packaging
  Exit Criteria:
    - Package builds successfully
    - Model package available in AI model registry

Phase 2: Unit Test
  Exit Criteria:
    - Model logic is correct
    - Model latency within KR (key result)
    - Model inference API is correctMethod: Launchpad

Phase 3: Validate Deployment Setup
  Exit Criteria:
    - Model artifact deployed from ML Registry to TeamServe endpoint
    - TeamServe endpoint is running
    - Model passes initialization health check
    - Searcher authorized for endpoint- Searcher deployed with correct configMethod: QD, Scraper

Phase 4: Integration Validation
  Exit Criteria:
    - Model scores match expected on test set
    - End-to-end latency within KR
  Method: Scraper, Autoscraper, Perfhammer

Phase 5: Experimentation
  Gate Conditions:
    - Experimentation capacity available
    - Pause if SLO breach (reliability, latency)Method: Monitor metrics

Phase 6: Production Launch
  Gate Conditions:
    - Model pre-launch checklist FILLED
    - Production capacity available
```

### How it applies
This provides the test_plan section's structure — a phased approach with explicit gates:

```yaml
test_plan:
  phases:
    - name: unit_validation
      method: launchpad
      exit_criteria:
        - model_logic_correct: true
        - latency_within_kr: true
        - api_contract_valid: true
    - name: integration_validation
      method: [scraper, perfhammer]
      exit_criteria:
        - scores_match_expected: threshold_0.95
        - e2e_latency_p99: <=200ms
    - name: canary_experiment
      method: statsig_experiment
      gate_conditions:
        - capacity_available: true
        - slo_breach: falserollback_trigger: slo_breach
```

### Source
- [How To: Deploy ML Models to TEAMServe](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120204aa07fe7450f489899b60900ad6a0967/pages/5959589965/How+To+Deploy+ML+Models+to+TEAMServe)
- [[RFC]TeamServe Readiness Criteria for Search at Scale](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRCA/pages/5906210553/RFC+TeamServe+Readiness+Criteria+for+Search+at+Scale)

