## Finding 7: Post-Deployment Monitoring Schema

### What it is
A structured specification for what must be monitored after an ML model deployment, including health sources, verification methods, and alert configurations.

### How it works
From multiple Atlassian sources including Safe Release, Harness PDV, and ML Lens:

**Atlassian Standard Requirements** (from "Standard - Safe & Reliable Code Rollouts"):
1. **R2**: All production deployments must utilize Post Deployment Verification (PDV) including:
   - Pollinator PDV Checks (Synthetics & Health/Deep checks)
   - Canary Analysis (statistical comparison of canary vs baseline)

**Post-deploy monitoring dimensions** for ML:

```yaml
post_deploy_monitoring:
  health_checks:
    - type: liveness
      endpoint: /healthcheck
      interval: 10s
      failure_threshold: 3
    - type: readiness
      endpoint: /deepcheck
      interval: 30s
      dependencies: [model_loaded, feature_store_connected]
    - type: inference_smoke
      endpoint: /v1/predict
      test_payload: "synthetic_golden_input"
      expected_output_schema: trueinterval: 60smetrics:
    latency:
      - p50, p90, p95, p99
      - per_endpoint_breakdown: true
      - baseline_comparison: <=1.1x
    throughput:
      - requests_per_second
      - tokens_per_second (for LLMs)
    errors:
      - error_rate_total
      - error_rate_by_type: [timeout, oom, model_error, input_validation]
      - circuit_breaker_state
    resources:
      - gpu_utilization
      - gpu_memory
      - cpu_utilization
      - memory_utilization
      - disk_utilization
    model_quality:
      - drift_score (KS/KL/cosine)
      - prediction_distribution_shift
      - feature_coverage- feature_freshness

  alerts:
    - name: high_error_rate
      condition: "error_rate > 0.1% for5m"
      severity: P1
      action: auto_rollback
    - name: latency_degradation
      condition: "p99> 2x baseline for 3m"
      severity: P2
      action: page_oncall
    - name: model_drift_detected
      condition: "drift_score > 0.05 for 1h"
      severity: P3
      action: create_retraining_ticket
    - name: gpu_saturation
      condition: "gpu_util > 90% for 10m"
      severity: P2
      action: scale_out

  verification_windows:
    canary: 2h
    regional_soak: 6h
    full_production: 24h
    
  dashboards:
    primary: "signalfx://ml-models/{model_name}"
    secondary: "ml-lens://models/{model_id}/drift"
    inference: "splunk://search index=ml_inference model={model_name}"
```

### How it applies
The post-deploy monitoring section forms a critical part of the deployment manifest — it must be specified BEFORE deployment and validated during the soak period.

### Source
- [Standard - Safe & Reliable Code Rollouts](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PMP/pages/6347889982/Standard+-+Safe+Reliable+Code+Rollouts)
- [PRD: Pre and Post deployment check](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~698094961/pages/7042666133/PRD+Pre+and+Post+deployment+check)
- [Platformized ML Observability - ML Lens: One Pager](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5362077533/Platformized+ML+Observability+-+ML+Lens+One+Pager)
- [Tier 1 - Post Deployment Verification](https://home.atlassian.com/o/2346a038-3c8c-498b-a79b-e7847859868d/s/a436116f-02ce-4520-8fbb-7301462a1674/goal/ATLAS-122260)

