Scope distinct from siblings: worker_2 covered responsible-ai-api patterns;
worker_3 the 13-tool coverage matrix; worker_4 the per-skill tool inventory;
worker_5 the §11.2 ORBIT-seed + §4.1 runbooks deep cadence. Worker_6 (this 
facet) consolidates the cross-cutting §4.1–§4.5 artifact inventory and adds
two layers the others did not surface (ADRs and dashboards).

Key contributions:

 1 Stable artifact ID scheme (RB-/QP-/EF-/TS-/RM-/ADR-/DB-) usable as a join
   key by the aggregator and every SKILL.md.
 2 Runbooks (RB-01..05) — 5 rows, cross-referenced summary of worker_5's deep
   breakdown.
 3 Query Patterns (QP-01..15) — primary contribution; 15 canonical query
   primitives across MLflow, Tecton/MLFS, ML Lens (KS / KL / embedding cosine
   / data-quality / model-perf / system-health), TEAMServe/Triton addressing,
   FinOps, cross-experiment correlation, similar-incident retrieval, lineage
   walk, reasoning-trace→PIR, per-tenant rate-limit.
 4 Eval Frameworks (EF-*) — 3 platforms (rovo-eval, AIX-eval, ML Lens) ×
   6-stage protocol (EF-PR-1..6: offline → adhoc → released → packaging →
   post-pkg verification → shadow/A-B → continuous monitoring) × 6
   non-negotiable standards (EF-NN-1..6: every-failure-case, mean±std
   multi-seed, slice-by-all-dims, full k-fold, calibration+CIs+fairness,
   mandatory ablation).
 5 Templates (TS-01..08) — Model Card, Experiment Report, Deployment Manifest,
   Architecture Comparison Report, Weekly Experiment Digest, Pre-analysis
   notebook, Reasoning trace, Auto-PIR.
 6 Reference Materials (RM-01..20 + RM-IND-01..04) — split into internal
   (overlaps §11.2) + industry.
 7 ADR layer (ADR-01..08) — promoted RFC-002, Policy for AI Agents in SDLC,
   AIF (PAI) L3-O1-KR1, Symphony fleet contract, 3-tier autonomy model,
   deployment-manifest mandate, uncertainty-handling contract,
   maturity-progression rule into machine-readable ADR rows for
   symphony-autonomy-check.
 8 Dashboards (DB-01..06) — explicit family enumeration (data-quality,
   model-performance, system-health, SignalFx SLO, FinOps, ML Artifact Cost)
   tied back to QP-* primitives.

Coverage roll-up: 13/15 query patterns and 5/8 templates require net-new tools
from the 13-tool build queue. Eval frameworks are entirely uncovered today.

Gaps flagged to aggregator:

 • QP-10 / DB-05 / DB-06 (FinOps cost) — not covered by any of the 13 proposed
   tools.
 • QP-15 (per-tenant rate-limit inspection) — required by SOP-3 but no tool
   owns it.
 • TS-05 (Weekly Experiment Digest) — produced regularly but no skill owns it;
   recommend lifting ml-stakeholder-reporting from prior role_setup run.
 • ADR-04 (Symphony fleet contract) — referenced operationally but no
   canonical source-of-truth doc named.
 • Runtime fairness/calibration overlay (EF-PR-6 × EF-NN-3/5) — ml-lens-query
   does drift only; the fairness/calibration runtime layer has no tool home.


Recommendations: adopt the ID scheme as a stable join key; treat 6-stage ×
6-standard as a matrix overlay in ml-evaluation-rigor; split ADRs from RMs
(machine-readable rows for symphony-autonomy-check); fill cost gap by either
lifting ml-cost-stewardship or extending ml-lens-query; bind RB-05 PIR
write-back via orbit-context-bind; reuse local
_dev/sre_skills_tools/skills/incident-response/SOPs/ structure as the starting
shape for the ML-specific ml-incident-response SOPs.
