## 2. Slicing Analysis

### What It Is
Disaggregated evaluation where model performance metrics are computed separately across meaningful subgroups (slices) of the evaluation set to reveal hidden performance disparities.

### How It Works

#### Pattern 1: Per-Slice Accuracy Reporting (Auto-Triage Agent)
From [Auto-Triage Agent: Evaluation & Metrics](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020c26b4615db3c4ab28b7fd51f4f23aae7/pages/6878919766):

**Method:**
1. Split evaluation set into N stratified slices (up to 200 tickets per class per slice)
2. Report per-slice metrics: Accuracy (matched), Accuracy (all), Precision, Recall, F1, Support
3. Compute deltas between model versions per slice
4. Flag slices with recall < 60% as "remaining challenges"

**Reporting format:**
| Slice | v18Accuracy (all) | v19 Accuracy (all) | Δ All |
|-------|-------------------|-------------------|-------|
| s1 | 53.85% | 94.07% | +40.22% |
| s7 | 64.62% | 70.55% | +5.93% |

Per-class within slice:
| Class | Precision | Recall | F1 | Support |
|-------|-----------|--------|----|---------| 
| AppliedAI.Search.Platform | 100.0% | 16.1% | 27.8% | 186 |

#### Pattern 2: Business Segmentation Analysis (Brain Model)
From [Brain Model Evaluation Considerations](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/5558575336):

**Slicing dimensions:**
- Business type (SMB vs Enterprise)
- User cohort (user type, job function, sub-function)
- Product/item type
- Evaluation level (user-level, entitlement-level, tenant-level)

**Purpose:** Determine whether separate models are needed for each segment and identify gaps for specific business types.

#### Pattern 3: Fairness-Oriented Slicing
From [AI fairness & data risks](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~70121eeecde7086e94a778d189b8b5d0a90f2/pages/5749449742):

**Practical guardrails:**
- Always report performance **by group** alongside overall score
- Compare **false positives/negatives** across groups
- Investigate large gaps
- Metrics to slice: precision, recall, F1, FPR, FNR

**Red flag:** "Only overall accuracy is reported; no group breakdowns."

#### Pattern 4: ML Lens Slice-and-Dice (Atlassian Internal)
From [Slice and Dice Training and Evaluation Metrics in ML Studio with ML Lens](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/blog/2025/10/28/6008049666):

**Capabilities:**
- `group_by` any categorical tag (e.g., `tenant_id`, `region`, `product`)
- Per-slice time-series visualization
- Cross-slice comparison on non-time-series axes (e.g., epoch)
- Drill-down from chart → specific run

#### Pattern 5: Threshold-Aware Slicing for Imbalanced Data
From [Evaluation Metrics Enhancement for Loss Function Experiments](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020e5c06a3880f04af68debb2e4dd3726e5/pages/6540156725):

**Problem:** Fixed threshold (0.5) masks performance for rare classes (0.4% positive rate → 0 recall at 0.5 threshold).

**Solution:** Per-task optimal threshold search + threshold-independent metrics:
- AUROC (discrimination across all thresholds)
-AUCPR (sensitive to minority class)
- F1_optimal + F1_threshold (best achievable F1 + what threshold achieves it)
- Precision_optimal, Recall_optimal

### How It Applies to a Skill/Tool

**For SKILL.md workflow:**
```
## Slicing Analysis Protocol
1. Define mandatory slicing dimensions:
   - Data-driven: class distribution, input length, complexity tier
   - Business-driven: tenant size, product, region
   - Fairness-driven: demographic groups (if applicable)
2. For EACH slice with≥30samples:
   a. Compute full metric suite (precision, recall, F1, AUROC)
   b. Compute threshold-independent metrics (AUROC, AUCPR)
   c. Find optimal operating point per slice
3. Compare across slices:
   - Max disparity = max(metric) - min(metric) across slices
   - Flag slices with recall < 60% or F1 < 0.5
4. GATE: If max disparity > 20pp in any primary metric → investigate before ship
5. Document in model card: per-slice performance table
```

**For tool operations:**
- `compute_sliced_metrics(eval_results, slice_dimensions, metrics_list)` → per-slice metric table
- `find_optimal_thresholds(predictions, labels, slices)` → per-slice threshold + metrics at optimal point
- `compute_disparity(sliced_metrics)` → max gap, mean gap, flagged slices
- `emit_to_ml_lens(sliced_metrics, run_id, tags)` → push to ML Lens for dashboarding

### Source
- Internal: Auto-Triage Agent Evaluation, Brain Model Evaluation, ML Lens documentation, Evaluation Metrics Enhancement page
- External: Google Fairness Indicators, TensorFlow Model Analysis slicing, scikit-learn classification_report per class

