## Original User Request
**Description**: Design and create the ML-Platform-native skill and tool set that powers the AI MLE's end-to-end production ML lifecycle on Atlassian's stack. This subtask covers the cohesive cluster of capabilities sharing ML Platform auth, APIs, and conventions (ML Studio, MLflow, ML Registry/Tarot v3, MLFS/Tecton, ML Lens, SignalFx, TEAMServe, SageMaker, AI Gateway, Launchpad, Symphony/ORBIT). Drivers from the role doc: §2 R1–R9, §4.1–§4.4, §5.1, §5.3, §6 SOP-1/SOP-2/SOP-3, §10.2, §11.1, §11.3.

Proposed SKILLS (workflow guidance leveraging existing + new tools):
  • `ml-experiment-lifecycle` — SOP-2 workflow: hypothesis → literature synthesis → pre-analysis → parallel variants → mandatory ablations → multi-seed eval → architecture comparison report. Cites §4.2, §6 SOP-2, §10.2.
  • `ml-drift-triggered-retraining` — SOP-1 workflow: drift signal correlation → reproduce baseline → parallel retrain → eval gating → canary → rollback. Cites §6 SOP-1.
  • `ml-incident-response` — SOP-3: circuit-breaker handling, cross-correlation, 30-min cadence comms, auto-PIR drafting. Cites §6 SOP-3, §4.1.
  • `ml-deployment-manifest` — Construct the non-negotiable manifest (intent, non-goals, invariants, risk, test plan, rollback, post-deploy monitoring) per §10.5, §7 row deploy.
  • `ml-launch-review-checklist` — Encodes the ML Launch Review Checklist as automated gates (§4.1, §2 R8).
  • `ml-runbook-authoring` — Template-driven runbook creation/refresh (§4.1, §11.3 task 2).
  • `ml-evaluation-rigor` — Enforces elevated standards: every-failure-case categorization, slicing, multi-seed mean±std, k-fold, calibration+CIs+fairness, ablation interactions (§4.2, §10.2).

Proposed TOOLS (new executable capabilities — only where no existing tool covers):
  • `mlflow-run` — Create/query MLflow runs with standardized run-name pattern, flattened params, per-segment metrics, model artifact logging (§3.1, §4.3).
  • `ml-registry-tarot` — Register/query/promote models in Tarot v3 with lineage + compliance metadata; read prior model versions for reproducibility (§2 R5, §11.1).
  • `ml-studio-job` — Launch/monitor training jobs and HPO sweeps (Optimus Prime / Bayesian) on ML Studio/Databricks/ML Fabric; capture convergence diagnostics (§2 R3, §5.1).
  • `feature-store-mlfs-tecton` — Read/write/audit features (coverage, freshness, sparsity by connector/region/tenant), check online/offline consistency (§2 R4, §4.3).
  • `ml-lens-query` — Query drift metrics (KS, KL, embedding cosine), data-quality and model-performance dashboards; subscribe to alerts (§4.3, §9).
  • `signalfx-detector-iac` — Author/update SignalFx detectors-as-code and per-endpoint SLOs in IaC (§2 R7, §11.3 task 6).
  • `teamserve-deploy` — Deploy/rollback/canary via TEAMServe gRPC + Micros service descriptors; verify post-deploy invariants (§5.1, §5.3).
  • `sagemaker-endpoint` — Manage SageMaker endpoints (GPU autoscaling, AZ rotation) for owned models (§5.1, §5.3).
  • `ai-gateway-routing` — Inspect/update AI Gateway routing config for OpenAI/Anthropic/Bedrock/Gemini/internal LLM routing (§3.2, §5.1).
  • `rovo-eval-runner` / `aix-eval-runner` — Trigger eval workflows and pull structured results (§4.2).
  • `pir-drafter` — Generate PIRs from reasoning traces with TTD/TTH/TTR/TTC, gaps, prevention, playbook updates within 5 BD (§6 SOP-3, §7.3).
  • `orbit-context-bind` — Read/write ORBIT context for owned model program(s); enrich on every task (§7.2, §10.4).
  • `symphony-autonomy-check` — Validate proposed action against 3-tier autonomy + RFC-002 L1–L5 policy pack (§10.5).

